delimiter $ ( $ $ ) $;

provable sort wff;

--| (_Note_: This inference rule and the next one, ~ idi , will normally never appear in a completed proof. It can be ignored if you are using this database to assist learning logic - please start with the statement ~ wn instead.) This is a technical inference to assist proof development. It provides a temporary way to add an independent subproof to a proof under development, for later assignment to a normal proof step. The metamath program's Proof Assistant requires proofs to be developed backwards from the conclusion with no gaps, and it has no mechanism that lets the user to work on isolated subproofs. This inference provides a workaround for this limitation. It can be inserted at any point in a proof to allow an independent subproof to be developed on the side, for later use as part of the final proof. _Instructions_: (1) Assign this inference to any unknown step in the proof. Typically, the last unknown step is the most convenient, since 'assign last' can be used. This step will be replicated in hypothesis a1ii.1, from where the development of the main proof can continue. (2) Develop the independent subproof backwards from hypothesis a1ii.2. If desired, use a 'let' command to pre-assign the conclusion of the independent subproof to a1ii.2. (3) After the independent subproof is complete, use 'improve all' to assign it automatically to an unknown step in the main proof that matches it. (4) After the entire proof is complete, use 'minimize *' to clean up (discard) all ~ a1ii references automatically. This inference was originally designed to assist importing partially completed Proof Worksheets from the mmj2 Proof Assistant GUI, but it can also be useful on its own. Interestingly, no axioms are required for its proof. (Contributed by NM, 7-Feb-2006.)
theorem a1ii (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ ph $;

--| Inference form of ~ id . This inference rule, which requires no axioms for its proof, is useful as a copy-paste mechanism during proof development in mmj2. It is normally not referenced in the final version of a proof, since it is always redundant and can be removed using the 'minimize *' command in the metamath program's Proof Assistant. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 31-Dec-2011.)
theorem idi (ph: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ph $;

--| If ` ph ` is a wff, so is ` -. ph ` or "not ` ph ` ." Part of the recursive definition of a wff (well-formed formula). Traditionally, Greek letters are used to represent wffs, and we follow this convention. In propositional calculus, we define only wffs built up from other wffs, i.e. there is no starting or "atomic" wff. Later, in predicate calculus, we will extend the basic wff definition by including atomic wffs ( ~ weq and ~ wel ).
term wn (ph: wff): wff;

--| If ` ph ` and ` ps ` are wff's, so is ` ( ph -> ps ) ` or " ` ph ` implies ` ps ` ." Part of the recursive definition of a wff. The left-hand wff is called the antecedent, and the right-hand wff is called the consequent. In the case of ` ( ph -> ( ps -> ch ) ) ` , the middle ` ps ` may be informally called either an antecedent or part of the consequent depending on context.
term wi (ph ps: wff): wff;

--| Axiom _Simp_. Axiom A1 of [Margaris] p. 49. One of the axioms of propositional calculus. This axiom is called _Simp_ or "the principle of simplification" in _Principia Mathematica_ (Theorem *2.02 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 100) because "it enables us to pass from the joint assertion of ` ph ` and ` ps ` to the assertion of ` ph ` simply." The theorems of propositional calculus are also called _tautologies_. Although classical propositional logic tautologies can be proved using truth tables, there is no similarly simple system for intuitionistic propositional logic, so proving tautologies from axioms is the preferred approach. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
axiom ax_1 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ph) $;

--| Axiom _Frege_. Axiom A2 of [Margaris] p. 49. This axiom "distributes" an antecedent over two consequents. This axiom was part of Frege's original system and is known as _Frege_ in the literature. It is also proved as Theorem *2.77 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. The other direction of this axiom also turns out to be true, as demonstrated by ~ pm5.41 . (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
axiom ax_2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch)) $;

--| Rule of Modus Ponens. The postulated inference rule of propositional calculus. See e.g. Rule 1 of [Hamilton] p. 73. The rule says, "if ` ph ` is true, and ` ph ` implies ` ps ` , then ` ps ` must also be true." This rule is sometimes called "detachment," since it detaches the minor premise from the major premise. Note: In some web page displays such as the Statement List, the symbols "&" and "=>" informally indicate the relationship between the hypotheses and the assertion (conclusion), abbreviating the English words "and" and "implies." They are not part of the formal language. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
axiom ax_mp (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ ps $;

--| A double modus ponens inference. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 24-Jan-2013.)
theorem mp2b (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ ch $;

--| Inference derived from axiom ~ ax-1 . See ~ a1d for an explanation of our informal use of the terms "inference" and "deduction." See also the comment in ~ syld . (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem a1i (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi ps ph $;

--| Drop and replace an antecedent. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 29-Jan-2015.)
theorem mp1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch ps $;

--| Inference derived from axiom ~ ax-2 . (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem a2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch) $;

--| Inference adding common antecedents in an implication. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem imim2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wi ch ph) (wi ch ps) $;

--| A modus ponens deduction. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem mpd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| An inference version of the transitive laws for implication ~ imim2 and ~ imim1 , which Russell and Whitehead call "the principle of the syllogism...because...the syllogism in Barbara is derived from them" (quote after Theorem *2.06 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 101). Some authors call this law a "hypothetical syllogism." (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 20-Oct-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 26-Jul-2012.)
theorem syl (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| A nested modus ponens inference. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Stefan Allan, 20-Mar-2006.)
theorem mpi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| A double modus ponens inference. (Contributed by NM, 5-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Jul-2013.)
theorem mp2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ ch $;

--| Inference chaining two syllogisms. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem _3syl (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Inference chaining three syllogisms. The use of this theorem is marked "discouraged" because it can cause the "minimize" command to have very long run times. However, feel free to use "minimize 4syl /override" if you wish. (Contributed by BJ, 14-Jul-2018.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem _4syl (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi th ta $ >
  $ wi ph ta $;

--| Principle of identity. Theorem *2.08 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 101. For another version of the proof directly from axioms, see ~ idALT . (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Stefan Allan, 20-Mar-2006.)
theorem id (ph: wff):
  $ wi ph ph $;

--| Principle of identity. Theorem *2.08 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 101. This version is proved directly from the axioms for demonstration purposes. This proof is a popular example in the literature and is identical, step for step, to the proofs of Theorem 1 of [Margaris] p. 51, Example 2.7(a) of [Hamilton] p. 31, Lemma 10.3 of [BellMachover] p. 36, and Lemma 1.8 of [Mendelson] p. 36. It is also "Our first proof" in Hirst and Hirst's _A Primer for Logic and Proof_ p. 17 (PDF p. 23) at ~ http://www.mathsci.appstate.edu/~~jlh/primer/hirst.pdf . For a shorter version of the proof that takes advantage of previously proved theorems, see ~ id . (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof modification is discouraged.) Use ~ id instead. (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem idALT (ph: wff):
  $ wi ph ph $;

--| Principle of identity with antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 26-Nov-1995.)
theorem idd (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ps) $;

--| Deduction introducing an embedded antecedent. (The proof was revised by Stefan Allan, 20-Mar-2006.) _Naming convention_: We often call a theorem a "deduction" and suffix its label with "d" whenever the hypotheses and conclusion are each prefixed with the same antecedent. This allows us to use the theorem in places where (in traditional textbook formalizations) the standard Deduction Theorem would be used; here ` ph ` would be replaced with a conjunction ( ~ wa ) of the hypotheses of the would-be deduction. By contrast, we tend to call the simpler version with no common antecedent an "inference" and suffix its label with "i"; compare theorem ~ a1i . Finally, a "theorem" would be the form with no hypotheses; in this case the "theorem" form would be the original axiom ~ ax-1 . We usually show the theorem form without a suffix on its label (e.g. ~ pm2.43 vs. ~ pm2.43i vs. ~ pm2.43d ). (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Revised by NM, 20-Mar-2006.)
theorem a1d (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch ps) $;

--| Deduction distributing an embedded antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 23-Jun-1994.)
theorem a2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wi ps ch) (wi ps th)) $;

--| Add two antecedents to a wff. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 4-Aug-2009.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Jul-2013.)
theorem _2a1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $;

--| Syllogism inference with commutation of antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 29-Aug-2004.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 2-Feb-2006.) (Proof shortened by Stefan Allan, 23-Feb-2006.)
theorem sylcom (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| Syllogism inference with commuted antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 24-May-2005.)
theorem syl5com (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $;

--| Inference that swaps (commutes) antecedents in an implication. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 4-Aug-2012.)
theorem com12 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ph ch) $;

--| A syllogism rule of inference. The second premise is used to replace the second antecedent of the first premise. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-May-2013.)
theorem syl5 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ph th) $;

--| A syllogism rule of inference. The second premise is used to replace the consequent of the first premise. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 30-Jul-2012.)
theorem syl6 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| Combine ~ syl5 and ~ syl6 . (Contributed by NM, 14-Nov-2013.)
theorem syl56 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi th ta $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ph ta) $;

--| Syllogism inference with commuted antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 25-May-2005.)
theorem syl6com (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ph th) $;

--| Modus ponens inference with commutation of antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 17-Mar-1996.)
theorem mpcom (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ps ph $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ps ch $;

--| Syllogism inference with common nested antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 4-Nov-2004.)
theorem syli (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ps (wi ph ch) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ph th) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ph th) $;

--| Replace two antecedents. Implication-only version of ~ syl2an . (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 14-May-2013.)
theorem syl2im (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi ps (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch ta) $;

--| This theorem, called "Assertion," can be thought of as closed form of modus ponens ~ ax-mp . Theorem *2.27 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 104. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem pm2_27 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wi ph ps) ps) $;

--| A nested modus ponens deduction. (Contributed by NM, 12-Dec-2004.)
theorem mpdd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A nested modus ponens deduction. (Contributed by NM, 14-Dec-2004.)
theorem mpid (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A nested modus ponens deduction. (Contributed by NM, 16-Apr-2005.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 15-Jan-2008.)
theorem mpdi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A doubly nested modus ponens inference. (Contributed by NM, 31-Dec-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 31-Jul-2012.)
theorem mpii (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| Syllogism deduction. Notice that ~ syld has the same form as ~ syl with ` ph ` added in front of each hypothesis and conclusion. When all theorems referenced in a proof are converted in this way, we can replace ` ph ` with a hypothesis of the proof, allowing the hypothesis to be eliminated with ~ id and become an antecedent. The Deduction Theorem for propositional calculus, e.g. Theorem 3 in [Margaris] p. 56, tells us that this procedure is always possible. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 19-Feb-2008.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Aug-2012.)
theorem syld (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A double modus ponens deduction. (Contributed by NM, 23-May-2013.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Jul-2013.)
theorem mp2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Deduction introducing a nested embedded antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 17-Dec-2004.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 15-Jan-2008.)
theorem a1dd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi th ch)) $;

--| Inference absorbing redundant antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 28-Nov-2008.)
theorem pm2_43i (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ph ps) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Deduction absorbing redundant antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 28-Nov-2008.)
theorem pm2_43d (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ps ch)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $;

--| Inference absorbing redundant antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 7-Nov-1995.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 28-Nov-2008.)
theorem pm2_43a (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ps (wi ph (wi ps ch)) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ph ch) $;

--| Inference absorbing redundant antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 31-Oct-1995.)
theorem pm2_43b (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ps (wi ph (wi ps ch)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $;

--| Absorption of redundant antecedent. Also called the "Contraction" or "Hilbert" axiom. Theorem *2.43 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 106. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 15-Aug-2004.)
theorem pm2_43 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph (wi ph ps)) (wi ph ps) $;

--| Deduction adding nested antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem imim2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wi th ps) (wi th ch)) $;

--| A closed form of syllogism (see ~ syl ). Theorem *2.05 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 100. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 6-Sep-2012.)
theorem imim2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi (wi ch ph) (wi ch ps)) $;

--| Deduction embedding an antecedent. (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 4-Oct-2013.)
theorem embantd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wi ps ch) th) $;

--| Triple syllogism deduction. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 4-Aug-2009.)
theorem _3syld (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ta) $;

--| Virtual deduction rule. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 20-Apr-2011.)
theorem sylsyld (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch ta) $;

--| Inference joining two implications. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 29-Oct-2011.)
theorem imim12i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi (wi ps ch) (wi ph th) $;

--| Inference adding common consequents in an implication, thereby interchanging the original antecedent and consequent. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 4-Aug-2012.)
theorem imim1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wi ps ch) (wi ph ch) $;

--| Inference adding three nested antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 19-Dec-2006.)
theorem imim3i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wi th ph) (wi (wi th ps) (wi th ch)) $;

--| A syllogism inference combined with contraction. (Contributed by NM, 4-May-1994.) (Revised by NM, 13-Jul-2013.)
theorem sylc (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| A syllogism inference combined with contraction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 7-Jul-2011.)
theorem syl3c (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta)) $ >
  $ wi ph ta $;

--| ~ syl6 combined with ~ mpi . (Contributed by Alan Sare, 8-Jul-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 13-Sep-2012.)
theorem syl6mpi (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ th $ >
  $ wi ch (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ta) $;

--| Modus ponens combined with a syllogism inference. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 20-Apr-2011.)
theorem mpsyl (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ps th $;

--| Inference combining ~ syl6 with contraction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 2-May-2011.)
theorem syl6c (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ta) $;

--| Nested syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 12-Dec-2004.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 11-May-2013.)
theorem syldd (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi th ta)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch ta)) $;

--| A nested syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Josh Purinton, 29-Dec-2000.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 2-Feb-2006.)
theorem syl5d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th (wi ch ta)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th (wi ps ta)) $;

--| A syllogism rule of inference. The second premise is used to replace the third antecedent of the first premise. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Aug-2012.)
theorem syl7 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wi th (wi ps ta)) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi th (wi ph ta)) $;

--| A nested syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Josh Purinton, 29-Dec-2000.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 2-Feb-2006.) (Revised by NM, 3-Feb-2006.)
theorem syl6d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch ta)) $;

--| A syllogism rule of inference. The second premise is used to replace the consequent of the first premise. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Aug-2012.)
theorem syl8 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi th ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch ta)) $;

--| A nested syllogism inference with different antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Josh Purinton, 29-Dec-2000.)
theorem syl9 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ch ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th (wi ps ta)) $;

--| A nested syllogism inference with different antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl9r (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ch ta) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ph (wi ps ta)) $;

--| Deduction combining antecedents and consequents. (Contributed by NM, 7-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 30-Oct-2011.)
theorem imim12d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wi ch th) (wi ps ta)) $;

--| Deduction adding nested consequents. (Contributed by NM, 3-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 12-Sep-2012.)
theorem imim1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wi ch th) (wi ps th)) $;

--| A closed form of syllogism (see ~ syl ). Theorem *2.06 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 100. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-May-2013.)
theorem imim1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi (wi ps ch) (wi ph ch)) $;

--| Theorem *2.83 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm2_83 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi (wi ph (wi ch th)) (wi ph (wi ps th))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Swap 2nd and 3rd. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 4-Aug-2012.)
theorem com23 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch (wi ps th)) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Rotate right. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.)
theorem com3r (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ph (wi ps th)) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Swap 1st and 3rd. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 28-Jul-2012.)
theorem com13 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ps (wi ph th)) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Rotate left. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 28-Jul-2012.)
theorem com3l (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ch (wi ph th)) $;

--| Swap antecedents. Theorem *2.04 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 100. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 12-Sep-2012.)
theorem pm2_04 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi ps (wi ph ch)) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Swap 3rd and 4th. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.)
theorem com34 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi th (wi ch ta))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Rotate left. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by O'Cat, 15-Aug-2004.)
theorem com4l (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ph ta))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Rotate twice. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.)
theorem com4t (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi th (wi ph (wi ps ta))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Rotate right. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.)
theorem com4r (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ph (wi ps (wi ch ta))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Swap 2nd and 4th. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 28-Jul-2012.)
theorem com24 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th (wi ch (wi ps ta))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Swap 1st and 4th. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 28-Jul-2012.)
theorem com14 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ps (wi ch (wi ph ta))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Swap 4th and 5th. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 28-Jun-2009.)
theorem com45 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi ta (wi th et)))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Swap 3rd and 5th. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 28-Jun-2009.)
theorem com35 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ta (wi th (wi ch et)))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Swap 2nd and 5th. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 28-Jun-2009.)
theorem com25 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ta (wi ch (wi th (wi ps et)))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Rotate left. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 28-Jun-2009.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 29-Jul-2012.)
theorem com5l (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta (wi ph et)))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Swap 1st and 5th. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 28-Jun-2009.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 29-Jul-2012.)
theorem com15 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi ta (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ph et)))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Rotate left twice. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 28-Jun-2009.)
theorem com52l (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi th (wi ta (wi ph (wi ps et)))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Rotate right twice. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 28-Jun-2009.)
theorem com52r (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ta (wi ph (wi ps (wi ch et)))) $;

--| Commutation of antecedents. Rotate right. (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 29-Jul-2012.)
theorem com5r (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi ta (wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th et)))) $;

--| Elimination of a nested antecedent. (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 9-May-2013.)
theorem jarr (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wi ph ps) ch) (wi ps ch) $;

--| Inference based on ~ pm2.86 . (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Apr-2013.)
theorem pm2_86i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $;

--| Deduction based on ~ pm2.86 . (Contributed by NM, 29-Jun-1995.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Apr-2013.)
theorem pm2_86d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wi ps ch) (wi ps th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $;

--| Converse of axiom ~ ax-2 . Theorem *2.86 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 108. (Contributed by NM, 25-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Apr-2013.)
theorem pm2_86 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch)) (wi ph (wi ps ch)) $;

--| The Linearity Axiom of the infinite-valued sentential logic (L-infinity) of Lukasiewicz. (Contributed by O'Cat, 12-Aug-2004.)
theorem loolin (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wi ph ps) (wi ps ph)) (wi ps ph) $;

--| An alternate for the Linearity Axiom of the infinite-valued sentential logic (L-infinity) of Lukasiewicz, due to Barbara Wozniakowska, _Reports on Mathematical Logic_ 10, 129-137 (1978). (Contributed by O'Cat, 8-Aug-2004.)
theorem loowoz (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch)) (wi (wi ps ph) (wi ps ch)) $;

--| Extend wff definition to include conjunction ('and').
term wa (ph ps: wff): wff;

--| Extend our wff definition to include the biconditional connective.
term wb (ph ps: wff): wff;

--| Left 'and' elimination. One of the axioms of propositional logic. Use its alias ~ simpl instead for naming consistency with set.mm. (New usage is discouraged.) (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-Jan-2015.)
axiom ax_ia1 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ph $;

--| Right 'and' elimination. One of the axioms of propositional logic. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-Jan-2015.) Use its alias ~ simpr instead for naming consistency with set.mm. (New usage is discouraged.)
axiom ax_ia2 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ps $;

--| 'And' introduction. One of the axioms of propositional logic. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 31-Jan-2015.)
axiom ax_ia3 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa ph ps)) $;

--| Elimination of a conjunct. Theorem *3.26 (Simp) of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 112. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 13-Nov-2012.)
theorem simpl (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ph $;

--| Elimination of a conjunct. Theorem *3.27 (Simp) of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 112. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 13-Nov-2012.)
theorem simpr (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ps $;

--| Inference eliminating a conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 15-Jun-1994.)
theorem simpli (ph ps: wff):
  $ wa ph ps $ >
  $ ph $;

--| Deduction eliminating a conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem simpld (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wa ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Inference eliminating a conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 15-Jun-1994.)
theorem simpri (ph ps: wff):
  $ wa ph ps $ >
  $ ps $;

--| Deduction eliminating a conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 3-Oct-2013.)
theorem simprd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wa ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Exportation inference. (This theorem used to be labeled "exp" but was changed to "ex" so as not to conflict with the math token "exp", per the June 2006 Metamath spec change.) (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Eric Schmidt, 22-Dec-2006.)
theorem ex (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $;

--| Exportation inference with commuted antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 25-May-2005.)
theorem expcom (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ph ch) $;

--| This is our first definition, which introduces and defines the biconditional connective ` <-> ` . We define a wff of the form ` ( ph <-> ps ) ` as an abbreviation for ` ( ( ph -> ps ) /\ ( ps -> ph ) ) ` . Unlike most traditional developments, we have chosen not to have a separate symbol such as "Df." to mean "is defined as." Instead, we will later use the biconditional connective for this purpose, as it allows us to use logic to manipulate definitions directly. For an example of such a definition, see ~ df-3or . This greatly simplifies many proofs since it eliminates the need for a separate mechanism for introducing and eliminating definitions. Of course, we cannot use this mechanism to define the biconditional itself, since it hasn't been introduced yet. Instead, we use a more general form of definition, described as follows. In its most general form, a definition is simply an assertion that introduces a new symbol (or a new combination of existing symbols, as in ~ df-3an ) that is eliminable and does not strengthen the existing language. The latter requirement means that the set of provable statements not containing the new symbol (or new combination) should remain exactly the same after the definition is introduced. Our definition of the biconditional may look unusual compared to most definitions, but it strictly satisfies these requirements. The justification for our definition is that if we mechanically replace ` ( ph <-> ps ) ` (the definiendum i.e. the thing being defined) with ` ( ( ph -> ps ) /\ ( ps -> ph ) ) ` (the definiens i.e. the defining expression) in the definition, the definition becomes the previously proved theorem ~ biijust . It is impossible to use ~ df-bi to prove any statement expressed in the original language that can't be proved from the original axioms, because if we simply replace each instance of ~ df-bi in the proof with the corresponding ~ biijust instance, we will end up with a proof from the original axioms. Note that from Metamath's point of view, a definition is just another axiom - i.e. an assertion we claim to be true - but from our high level point of view, we are are not strengthening the language. To indicate this fact, we prefix definition labels with "df-" instead of "ax-". (This prefixing is an informal convention that means nothing to the Metamath proof verifier; it is just for human readability.) ~ df-bi itself is a conjunction of two implications (to avoid using the biconditional in its own definition), but once we have the biconditional, we can prove ~ dfbi2 which uses the biconditional instead. Other definitions of the biconditional, such as ~ dfbi3dc , only hold for decidable propositions, not all propositions. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Revised by Jim Kingdon, 24-Nov-2017.)
axiom df_bi (ph ps: wff):
  $ wa (wi (wb ph ps) (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ps ph))) (wi (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ps ph)) (wb ph ps)) $;

--| Property of the biconditional connective. (Contributed by NM, 11-May-1999.) (Revised by NM, 31-Jan-2015.)
theorem bi1 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph ps) (wi ph ps) $;

--| Property of the biconditional connective. (Contributed by NM, 11-May-1999.)
theorem bi3 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi (wi ps ph) (wb ph ps)) $;

--| Infer an implication from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem biimpi (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference from a biconditional and an implication. Useful for substituting an antecedent with a definition. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem sylbi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Eric Schmidt, 22-Dec-2006.)
theorem imp (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $;

--| Importation inference with commuted antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 25-May-2005.)
theorem impcom (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ph) ch $;

--| Infer an equivalence from an implication and its converse. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem impbii (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ps ph $ >
  $ wb ph ps $;

--| Deduce an equivalence from two implications. (Contributed by Rodolfo Medina, 12-Oct-2010.)
theorem impbidd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi th ch)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wb ch th)) $;

--| Deduce an equivalence from two implications. (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 12-May-2013.)
theorem impbid21d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ps (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wb ch th)) $;

--| Deduce an equivalence from two implications. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Revised by Wolf Lammen, 3-Nov-2012.)
theorem impbid (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch ps) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $;

--| Property of the biconditional connective. (Contributed by NM, 11-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 11-Nov-2012.)
theorem bi2 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph ps) (wi ps ph) $;

--| Commutative law for equivalence. (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 10-Nov-2012.)
theorem bicom1 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph ps) (wb ps ph) $;

--| Inference from commutative law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Revised by NM, 16-Sep-2013.)
theorem bicomi (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ps ph $;

--| Infer a converse implication from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 16-Sep-2013.)
theorem biimpri (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wi ps ph $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference from a biconditional and an implication. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem sylbir (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ps ph $ >
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Join antecedents with conjunction. Theorem *3.2 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 111. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 12-Nov-2012.) (Proof shortened by Jia Ming, 17-Nov-2020.)
theorem pm3_2 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa ph ps)) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference from an implication and a biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem sylib (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wb ps ch $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Commutative law for equivalence. Theorem *4.21 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Revised by NM, 11-Nov-2012.)
theorem bicom (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wb ph ps) (wb ps ph) $;

--| Commute two sides of a biconditional in a deduction. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bicomd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch ps) $;

--| Infer an equivalence from two implications. (Contributed by NM, 6-Mar-2007.)
theorem impbid1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ch ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $;

--| Infer an equivalence from two implications. (Contributed by NM, 6-Mar-2007.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 27-Sep-2013.)
theorem impbid2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ps ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch ps) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $;

--| Deduce an implication from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem biimpd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $;

--| An inference from a biconditional, related to modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem mpbi (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ ps $;

--| An inference from a biconditional, related to modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem mpbir (ph ps: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ ph $;

--| A deduction from a biconditional, related to modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem mpbid (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| An inference from a nested biconditional, related to modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Oct-2012.)
theorem mpbii (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference from an implication and a biconditional. Useful for substituting a consequent with a definition. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem sylibr (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| A syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 3-Aug-1994.)
theorem sylibd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 3-Aug-1994.)
theorem sylbid (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A deduction from a biconditional, related to modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 9-Aug-1994.)
theorem mpbidi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi th (wi ph ps) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ph ch) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference from a nested implication and a biconditional. Useful for substituting an embedded antecedent with a definition. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl5bi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ph th) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference from a nested implication and a biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl5bir (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ps ph $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ph th) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl5ib (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ph th) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 19-Jun-2007.)
theorem syl5ibcom (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 3-Apr-1994.) (Revised by NM, 22-Sep-2013.)
theorem syl5ibr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ph ps) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 20-Jun-2007.)
theorem syl5ibrcom (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch ps) $;

--| Deduce a converse implication from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Sep-2013.)
theorem biimprd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch ps) $;

--| Deduce a commuted implication from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 3-May-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Sep-2013.)
theorem biimpcd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ph ch) $;

--| Deduce a converse commuted implication from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 3-May-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 20-Dec-2013.)
theorem biimprcd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ph ps) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference from a nested implication and a biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl6ib (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference from a nested implication and a biconditional. Useful for substituting an embedded consequent with a definition. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl6ibr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wb th ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 2-Jan-1994.)
theorem syl6bi (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 18-May-1994.)
theorem syl6bir (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ch ps) $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference from a doubly nested implication and a biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl7bi (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wi th (wi ps ta)) $ >
  $ wi ch (wi th (wi ph ta)) $;

--| A syllogism rule of inference. The second premise is used to replace the consequent of the first premise. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1994.)
theorem syl8ib (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wb th ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch ta)) $;

--| A deduction from a biconditional, related to modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem mpbird (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| An inference from a nested biconditional, related to modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Oct-2012.)
theorem mpbiri (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| A syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 3-Aug-1994.)
theorem sylibrd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 3-Aug-1994.)
theorem sylbird (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ch ps) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| Principle of identity for logical equivalence. Theorem *4.2 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem biid (ph: wff):
  $ wb ph ph $;

--| Principle of identity with antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 25-Nov-1995.)
theorem biidd (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ps) $;

--| Two propositions are equivalent if they are both true. Closed form of ~ 2th . Equivalent to a ~ bi1 -like version of the xor-connective. This theorem stays true, no matter how you permute its operands. This is evident from its sharper version ` ( ph <-> ( ps <-> ( ph <-> ps ) ) ) ` . (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 12-May-2013.)
theorem pm5_1im (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wb ph ps)) $;

--| Two truths are equivalent. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1993.)
theorem _2th (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wb ph ps $;

--| Two truths are equivalent (deduction rule). (Contributed by NM, 3-Jun-2012.) (Revised by NM, 29-Jan-2013.)
theorem _2thd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $;

--| Inference that converts a biconditional implied by one of its arguments, into an implication. (Contributed by NM, 17-Oct-2003.)
theorem ibi (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ph ps) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Inference that converts a biconditional implied by one of its arguments, into an implication. (Contributed by NM, 22-Jul-2004.)
theorem ibir (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ph) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Deduction that converts a biconditional implied by one of its arguments, into an implication. (Contributed by NM, 26-Jun-2004.)
theorem ibd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wb ps ch)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional. Theorem *5.74 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 11-Apr-2013.)
theorem pm5_74 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wb ps ch)) (wb (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch)) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (inference rule). (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1994.)
theorem pm5_74i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (reverse inference rule). (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1994.)
theorem pm5_74ri (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (deduction rule). (Contributed by NM, 21-Mar-1996.)
theorem pm5_74d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wb ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wi ps ch) (wi ps th)) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (deduction rule). (Contributed by NM, 19-Mar-1997.)
theorem pm5_74rd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb (wi ps ch) (wi ps th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wb ch th)) $;

--| An inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 13-Oct-2012.)
theorem bitri (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ps ch $ >
  $ wb ph ch $;

--| An inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bitr2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ps ch $ >
  $ wb ch ph $;

--| An inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bitr3i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ps ph $ >
  $ wb ps ch $ >
  $ wb ph ch $;

--| An inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bitr4i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch ps $ >
  $ wb ph ch $;

--| Deduction form of ~ bitri . (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Apr-2013.)
theorem bitrd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps th) $;

--| Deduction form of ~ bitr2i . (Contributed by NM, 9-Jun-2004.)
theorem bitr2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ps) $;

--| Deduction form of ~ bitr3i . (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bitr3d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch th) $;

--| Deduction form of ~ bitr4i . (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bitr4d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps th) $;

--| A syllogism inference from two biconditionals. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl5bb (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ph th) $;

--| A syllogism inference from two biconditionals. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl5rbb (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wb th ph) $;

--| A syllogism inference from two biconditionals. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl5bbr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ps ph $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ph th) $;

--| A syllogism inference from two biconditionals. (Contributed by NM, 25-Nov-1994.)
theorem syl5rbbr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ps ph $ >
  $ wi ch (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ch (wb th ph) $;

--| A syllogism inference from two biconditionals. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl6bb (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps th) $;

--| A syllogism inference from two biconditionals. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl6rbb (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ps) $;

--| A syllogism inference from two biconditionals. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem syl6bbr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wb th ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps th) $;

--| A syllogism inference from two biconditionals. (Contributed by NM, 25-Nov-1994.)
theorem syl6rbbr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wb th ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ps) $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference, useful for removing a definition from both sides of an implication. (Contributed by NM, 10-Aug-1994.)
theorem _3imtr3i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wb ph ch $ >
  $ wb ps th $ >
  $ wi ch th $;

--| A mixed syllogism inference, useful for applying a definition to both sides of an implication. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem _3imtr4i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch ph $ >
  $ wb th ps $ >
  $ wi ch th $;

--| More general version of ~ 3imtr3i . Useful for converting conditional definitions in a formula. (Contributed by NM, 8-Apr-1996.)
theorem _3imtr3d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $;

--| More general version of ~ 3imtr4i . Useful for converting conditional definitions in a formula. (Contributed by NM, 26-Oct-1995.)
theorem _3imtr4d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ps) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ta ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $;

--| More general version of ~ 3imtr3i . Useful for converting definitions in a formula. (Contributed by NM, 20-May-1996.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 20-Dec-2013.)
theorem _3imtr3g (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wb ps th $ >
  $ wb ch ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $;

--| More general version of ~ 3imtr4i . Useful for converting definitions in a formula. (Contributed by NM, 20-May-1996.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 20-Dec-2013.)
theorem _3imtr4g (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wb th ps $ >
  $ wb ta ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $;

--| A chained inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem _3bitri (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ps ch $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb ph th $;

--| A chained inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2006.)
theorem _3bitrri (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ps ch $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb th ph $;

--| A chained inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2006.)
theorem _3bitr2i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb ph th $;

--| A chained inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2006.)
theorem _3bitr2ri (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb th ph $;

--| A chained inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 19-Aug-1993.)
theorem _3bitr3i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ph ch $ >
  $ wb ps th $ >
  $ wb ch th $;

--| A chained inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem _3bitr3ri (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ph ch $ >
  $ wb ps th $ >
  $ wb th ch $;

--| A chained inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. This inference is frequently used to apply a definition to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem _3bitr4i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch ph $ >
  $ wb th ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $;

--| A chained inference from transitive law for logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 2-Sep-1995.)
theorem _3bitr4ri (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch ph $ >
  $ wb th ps $ >
  $ wb th ch $;

--| Deduction from transitivity of biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 13-Aug-1999.)
theorem _3bitrd (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ta) $;

--| Deduction from transitivity of biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2006.)
theorem _3bitrrd (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ta ps) $;

--| Deduction from transitivity of biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2006.)
theorem _3bitr2d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps ta) $;

--| Deduction from transitivity of biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2006.)
theorem _3bitr2rd (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ta ps) $;

--| Deduction from transitivity of biconditional. Useful for converting conditional definitions in a formula. (Contributed by NM, 24-Apr-1996.)
theorem _3bitr3d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $;

--| Deduction from transitivity of biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2006.)
theorem _3bitr3rd (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ta th) $;

--| Deduction from transitivity of biconditional. Useful for converting conditional definitions in a formula. (Contributed by NM, 18-Oct-1995.)
theorem _3bitr4d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ps) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ta ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $;

--| Deduction from transitivity of biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2006.)
theorem _3bitr4rd (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ps) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ta ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ta th) $;

--| More general version of ~ 3bitr3i . Useful for converting definitions in a formula. (Contributed by NM, 4-Jun-1995.)
theorem _3bitr3g (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wb ps th $ >
  $ wb ch ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $;

--| More general version of ~ 3bitr4i . Useful for converting definitions in a formula. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem _3bitr4g (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wb th ps $ >
  $ wb ta ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $;

--| Construct a biconditional in antecedent position. (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 14-May-2013.)
theorem bi3ant (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wi (wi th ta) ph) (wi (wi (wi ta th) ps) (wi (wb th ta) ch)) $;

--| Express symmetries of theorems in terms of biconditionals. (Contributed by Wolf Lammen, 14-May-2013.)
theorem bisym (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wi ph ps) (wi ch th)) (wi (wi (wi ps ph) (wi th ch)) (wi (wb ph ps) (wb ch th))) $;

--| Introduce an antecedent to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 6-Feb-2013.)
theorem imbi2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wi ch ph) (wi ch ps) $;

--| Inference adding a biconditional to the left in an equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 16-May-2013.)
theorem bibi2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wb ch ph) (wb ch ps) $;

--| Inference adding a biconditional to the right in an equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bibi1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wb ph ch) (wb ps ch) $;

--| The equivalence of two equivalences. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bibi12i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb (wb ph ch) (wb ps th) $;

--| Deduction adding an antecedent to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem imbi2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wi th ps) (wi th ch)) $;

--| Deduction adding a consequent to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 17-Sep-2013.)
theorem imbi1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wi ps th) (wi ch th)) $;

--| Deduction adding a biconditional to the left in an equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-May-2013.)
theorem bibi2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wb th ps) (wb th ch)) $;

--| Deduction adding a biconditional to the right in an equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bibi1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wb ps th) (wb ch th)) $;

--| Deduction joining two equivalences to form equivalence of implications. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem imbi12d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wi ps th) (wi ch ta)) $;

--| Deduction joining two equivalences to form equivalence of biconditionals. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bibi12d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wb ps th) (wb ch ta)) $;

--| Theorem *4.84 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 122. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem imbi1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph ps) (wb (wi ph ch) (wi ps ch)) $;

--| Theorem *4.85 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 122. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-May-2013.)
theorem imbi2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph ps) (wb (wi ch ph) (wi ch ps)) $;

--| Introduce a consequent to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 17-Sep-2013.)
theorem imbi1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wi ph ch) (wi ps ch) $;

--| Join two logical equivalences to form equivalence of implications. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem imbi12i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb (wi ph ch) (wi ps th) $;

--| Theorem *4.86 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 122. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem bibi1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph ps) (wb (wb ph ch) (wb ps ch)) $;

--| A wff is equivalent to itself with true antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jan-1996.)
theorem biimt (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wi ph ps)) $;

--| Theorem *5.5 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_5 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb (wi ph ps) ps) $;

--| Inference rule introducing a theorem as an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 11-Nov-2012.)
theorem a1bi (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wb ps (wi ph ps) $;

--| Theorem *5.501 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Revised by NM, 24-Jan-2013.)
theorem pm5_501 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wb ph ps)) $;

--| Implication in terms of implication and biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 31-Mar-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Jan-2013.)
theorem ibib (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wi ph (wb ph ps)) $;

--| Implication in terms of implication and biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 29-Apr-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 21-Dec-2013.)
theorem ibibr (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wi ph (wb ps ph)) $;

--| A wff is equivalent to its equivalence with truth. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 13-May-2011.)
theorem tbt (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wb ps (wb ps ph) $;

--| Logical equivalence of commuted antecedents. Part of Theorem *4.87 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 122. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem bi2_04 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi ps (wi ph ch)) $;

--| Antecedent absorption implication. Theorem *5.4 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem pm5_4 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wi ph ps)) (wi ph ps) $;

--| Distributive law for implication. Compare Theorem *5.41 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem imdi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch)) $;

--| Theorem *5.41 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 12-Oct-2012.)
theorem pm5_41 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wi ph ps) (wi ph ch)) (wi ph (wi ps ch)) $;

--| Simplify an implication between two implications when the antecedent of the first is a consequence of the antecedent of the second. The reverse form is useful in producing the successor step in induction proofs. (Contributed by Paul Chapman, 22-Jun-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Sep-2013.)
theorem imim21b (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wi ps ph) (wb (wi (wi ph ch) (wi ps th)) (wi ps (wi ch th))) $;

--| Importation deduction. (Contributed by NM, 31-Mar-1994.)
theorem impd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp31 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp32 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $;

--| Exportation deduction. (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-1993.)
theorem expd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $;

--| A deduction version of exportation, followed by importation. (Contributed by NM, 6-Sep-2008.)
theorem expdimp (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ch th) $;

--| Mixed importation/commutation inference. (Contributed by NM, 22-Jun-2013.)
theorem impancom (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) (wi ps th) $;

--| Theorem *3.3 (Exp) of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 112. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Mar-2013.)
theorem pm3_3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi (wa ph ps) ch) (wi ph (wi ps ch)) $;

--| Theorem *3.31 (Imp) of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 112. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Mar-2013.)
theorem pm3_31 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi (wa ph ps) ch) $;

--| Import-export theorem. Part of Theorem *4.87 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 122. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Mar-2013.)
theorem impexp (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wa ph ps) ch) (wi ph (wi ps ch)) $;

--| Join antecedents with conjunction. Theorem *3.21 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 111. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem pm3_21 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa ps ph)) $;

--| Theorem *3.22 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 111. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 13-Nov-2012.)
theorem pm3_22 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wa ps ph) $;

--| Commutative law for conjunction. Theorem *4.3 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 118. (Contributed by NM, 25-Jun-1998.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 4-Nov-2012.)
theorem ancom (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph ps) (wa ps ph) $;

--| Commutation of conjuncts in consequent. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 14-Aug-2009.)
theorem ancomd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wa ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ch ps) $;

--| Inference commuting conjunction in antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.)
theorem ancoms (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ph) ch $;

--| Deduction commuting conjunction in antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 12-Dec-2004.)
theorem ancomsd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ch ps) th) $;

--| Infer conjunction of premises. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem pm3_2i (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wa ph ps $;

--| Nested conjunction of antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem pm3_43i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi (wi ph ch) (wi ph (wa ps ch))) $;

--| Deduction eliminating a conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1998.)
theorem simplbi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph (wa ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Deduction eliminating a conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1998.)
theorem simprbi (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph (wa ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| Inference adding a conjunct to the right of an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 30-Aug-1993.)
theorem adantr (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) ps $;

--| Inference adding a conjunct to the left of an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 30-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Nov-2012.)
theorem adantl (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ch ph) ps $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to the left of an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 4-May-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 20-Dec-2012.)
theorem adantld (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa th ps) ch) $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to the right of an antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 4-May-1994.)
theorem adantrd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps th) ch) $;

--| Modus ponens conjoining dissimilar antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 1-Feb-2008.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem mpan9 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $;

--| A syllogism deduction with conjoined antecents. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 6-Apr-2013.)
theorem syldan (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) th $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Nov-2012.)
theorem sylan (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 18-May-1994.)
theorem sylanb (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 18-May-1994.)
theorem sylanbr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ps ph $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Nov-2012.)
theorem sylan2 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ph) th $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.)
theorem sylan2b (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ph) th $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-1994.)
theorem sylan2br (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ch ph $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ph) th $;

--| A double syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 31-Jan-1997.)
theorem syl2an (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ta ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ta) th $;

--| A double syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 17-Sep-2013.)
theorem syl2anr (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ta ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ta ph) th $;

--| A double syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 29-Jul-1999.)
theorem syl2anb (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ta ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ta) th $;

--| A double syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 29-Jul-1999.)
theorem syl2anbr (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wb ps ph $ >
  $ wb ch ta $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ta) th $;

--| A syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 15-Dec-2004.)
theorem syland (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ch th) ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps th) ta) $;

--| A syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 15-Dec-2004.)
theorem sylan2d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa th ch) ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa th ps) ta) $;

--| A syllogism deduction. (Contributed by NM, 15-Dec-2004.)
theorem syl2and (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ch ta) et) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps th) et) $;

--| Inference from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 3-May-1994.)
theorem biimpa (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $;

--| Inference from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 3-May-1994.)
theorem biimpar (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) ps $;

--| Inference from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 3-May-1994.)
theorem biimpac (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ph) ch $;

--| Inference from a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 3-May-1994.)
theorem biimparc (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ch ph) ps $;

--| Introduction of antecedent as conjunct. Theorem *4.73 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 121. (Contributed by NM, 30-Mar-1994.) (Revised by NM, 24-Mar-2013.)
theorem iba (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wa ps ph)) $;

--| Introduction of antecedent as conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 5-Dec-1995.) (Revised by NM, 24-Mar-2013.)
theorem ibar (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wa ph ps)) $;

--| A wff is equivalent to its conjunction with truth. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem biantru (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wb ps (wa ps ph) $;

--| A wff is equivalent to its conjunction with truth. (Contributed by NM, 3-Aug-1994.)
theorem biantrur (ph ps: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wb ps (wa ph ps) $;

--| A wff is equivalent to its conjunction with truth. (Contributed by NM, 2-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Oct-2013.)
theorem biantrud (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch (wa ch ps)) $;

--| A wff is equivalent to its conjunction with truth. (Contributed by NM, 1-May-1995.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem biantrurd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ch (wa ps ch)) $;

--| Deduce conjunction of the consequents of two implications ("join consequents with 'and'"). (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 25-Oct-2012.)
theorem jca (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ps ch) $;

--| Deduction conjoining the consequents of two implications. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Jul-2013.)
theorem jcad (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa ch th)) $;

--| Join three consequents. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 1-Aug-2009.)
theorem jca31 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ph (wa (wa ps ch) th) $;

--| Join three consequents. (Contributed by FL, 1-Aug-2009.)
theorem jca32 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ps (wa ch th)) $;

--| Deduction replacing implication with conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem jcai (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ps ch) $;

--| Inference conjoining a theorem to left of consequent in an implication. (Contributed by NM, 31-Dec-1993.)
theorem jctil (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ch ps) $;

--| Inference conjoining a theorem to right of consequent in an implication. (Contributed by NM, 31-Dec-1993.)
theorem jctir (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ps ch) $;

--| Inference conjoining a theorem to the left of a consequent. (Contributed by NM, 31-Dec-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Oct-2012.)
theorem jctl (ph ps: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ps ph) $;

--| Inference conjoining a theorem to the right of a consequent. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Oct-2012.)
theorem jctr (ph ps: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ph ps) $;

--| Deduction conjoining a theorem to left of consequent in an implication. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-2005.)
theorem jctild (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa th ch)) $;

--| Deduction conjoining a theorem to right of consequent in an implication. (Contributed by NM, 21-Apr-2005.)
theorem jctird (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa ch th)) $;

--| Conjoin antecedent to left of consequent. (Contributed by NM, 15-Aug-1994.)
theorem ancl (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi ph (wa ph ps)) $;

--| Conjoin antecedent to left of consequent. Theorem *4.7 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 25-Jul-1999.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Mar-2013.)
theorem anclb (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wi ph (wa ph ps)) $;

--| Theorem *5.42 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_42 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi ph (wi ps (wa ph ch))) $;

--| Conjoin antecedent to right of consequent. (Contributed by NM, 15-Aug-1994.)
theorem ancr (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ps) (wi ph (wa ps ph)) $;

--| Conjoin antecedent to right of consequent. (Contributed by NM, 25-Jul-1999.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Mar-2013.)
theorem ancrb (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wi ph (wa ps ph)) $;

--| Deduction conjoining antecedent to left of consequent. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1993.)
theorem ancli (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ph ps) $;

--| Deduction conjoining antecedent to right of consequent. (Contributed by NM, 15-Aug-1994.)
theorem ancri (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wa ps ph) $;

--| Deduction conjoining antecedent to left of consequent in nested implication. (Contributed by NM, 15-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 1-Nov-2012.)
theorem ancld (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa ps ch)) $;

--| Deduction conjoining antecedent to right of consequent in nested implication. (Contributed by NM, 15-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 1-Nov-2012.)
theorem ancrd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa ch ps)) $;

--| Conjoin antecedent to left of consequent in nested implication. (Contributed by NM, 10-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Jul-2013.)
theorem anc2l (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi ph (wi ps (wa ph ch))) $;

--| Conjoin antecedent to right of consequent in nested implication. (Contributed by NM, 15-Aug-1994.)
theorem anc2r (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi ph (wi ps (wa ch ph))) $;

--| Deduction conjoining antecedent to left of consequent in nested implication. (Contributed by NM, 10-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Dec-2012.)
theorem anc2li (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa ph ch)) $;

--| Deduction conjoining antecedent to right of consequent in nested implication. (Contributed by NM, 15-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Dec-2012.)
theorem anc2ri (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wa ch ph)) $;

--| Theorem *3.41 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 113. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm3_41 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ph ch) (wi (wa ph ps) ch) $;

--| Theorem *3.42 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 113. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm3_42 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wi ps ch) (wi (wa ph ps) ch) $;

--| Conjunction implies implication. Theorem *3.4 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 113. (Contributed by NM, 31-Jul-1995.)
theorem pm3_4 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ph ps) $;

--| Conjunction with implication. Compare Theorem *4.45 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 119. (Contributed by NM, 17-May-1998.)
theorem pm4_45im (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb ph (wa ph (wi ps ph)) $;

--| Conjoin antecedents and consequents in a deduction. (Contributed by NM, 3-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 18-Dec-2013.)
theorem anim12d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps th) (wa ch ta)) $;

--| Add a conjunct to right of antecedent and consequent in a deduction. (Contributed by NM, 3-Apr-1994.)
theorem anim1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps th) (wa ch th)) $;

--| Add a conjunct to left of antecedent and consequent in a deduction. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem anim2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa th ps) (wa th ch)) $;

--| Conjoin antecedents and consequents of two premises. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Dec-2013.)
theorem anim12i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) (wa ps th) $;

--| Variant of ~ anim12i with commutation. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.)
theorem anim12ci (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ch th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) (wa th ps) $;

--| Introduce conjunct to both sides of an implication. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem anim1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) (wa ps ch) $;

--| Introduce conjunct to both sides of an implication. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem anim2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ch ph) (wa ch ps) $;

--| Conjoin antecedents and consequents in a deduction. (Contributed by NM, 11-Nov-2007.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Jul-2013.)
theorem anim12ii (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ps ta) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph th) (wi ps (wa ch ta)) $;

--| Theorem *3.47 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 113. It was proved by Leibniz, and it evidently pleased him enough to call it 'praeclarum theorema' (splendid theorem). (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Apr-2013.)
theorem prth (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ch th)) (wi (wa ph ch) (wa ps th)) $;

--| Theorem *3.33 (Syll) of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 112. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm3_33 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ps ch)) (wi ph ch) $;

--| Theorem *3.34 (Syll) of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 112. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm3_34 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wi ps ch) (wi ph ps)) (wi ph ch) $;

--| Conjunctive detachment. Theorem *3.35 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 112. (Contributed by NM, 14-Dec-2002.)
theorem pm3_35 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wi ph ps)) ps $;

--| Theorem *5.31 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem pm5_31 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa ch (wi ph ps)) (wi ph (wa ps ch)) $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp4a (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi (wa ch th) ta)) $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp4b (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi (wa ch th) ta) $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp4c (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa (wa ps ch) th) ta) $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp4d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps (wa ch th)) ta) $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp41 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th) ta $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp42 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th) ta $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp43 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) (wa ch th)) ta $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp44 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wa ps ch) th)) ta $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem imp45 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps (wa ch th))) ta $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 7-Jul-2009.)
theorem imp5a (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi (wa th ta) et))) $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 7-Jul-2009.)
theorem imp5d (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) (wi (wa th ta) et) $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 7-Jul-2009.)
theorem imp5g (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi (wa (wa ch th) ta) et) $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 7-Jul-2009.)
theorem imp55 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph (wa ps (wa ch th))) ta) et $;

--| An importation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 7-Jul-2009.)
theorem imp511 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wa ps (wa ch th)) ta)) et $;

--| Exportation followed by a deduction version of importation. (Contributed by NM, 6-Sep-2008.)
theorem expimpd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp31 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp32 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp4a (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi (wa ch th) ta)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 23-Nov-2012.)
theorem exp4b (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi (wa ch th) ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp4c (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa (wa ps ch) th) ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp4d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps (wa ch th)) ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp41 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th) ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp42 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th) ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp43 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) (wa ch th)) ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp44 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa (wa ps ch) th)) ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by NM, 26-Apr-1994.)
theorem exp45 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps (wa ch th))) ta $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th ta))) $;

--| Export a wff from a right conjunct. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 30-Aug-2009.)
theorem expr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ch th) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 7-Jul-2009.)
theorem exp5c (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) (wi (wa th ta) et)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $;

--| An exportation inference. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 30-Aug-2009.)
theorem exp53 (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa ph ps) (wa ch th)) ta) et $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (wi th (wi ta et)))) $;

--| Export a wff from a left conjunct. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 28-Aug-2009.)
theorem expl (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $;

--| Import a wff into a right conjunct. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 30-Aug-2009.)
theorem impr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $;

--| Export a wff from a left conjunct. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 9-Jul-2014.)
theorem impl (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $;

--| Importation with conjunction in consequent. (Contributed by NM, 9-Aug-1994.)
theorem impac (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wa ch ps) $;

--| Inference form of ~ exbir . (Contributed by Alan Sare, 31-Dec-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 27-Jan-2013.)
theorem exbiri (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi th ch)) $;

--| Deduction eliminating a conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 22-Oct-2007.)
theorem simprbda (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wa ch th)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $;

--| Deduction eliminating a conjunct. (Contributed by NM, 22-Oct-2007.)
theorem simplbda (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wa ch th)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) th $;

--| Deduction eliminating a conjunct. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 31-Dec-2011.)
theorem simplbi2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph (wa ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi ch ph) $;

--| A theorem similar to the standard definition of the biconditional. Definition of [Margaris] p. 49. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Revised by NM, 31-Jan-2015.)
theorem dfbi2 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wb ph ps) (wa (wi ph ps) (wi ps ph)) $;

--| Implication in terms of biconditional and conjunction. Theorem *4.71 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 2-Dec-2012.)
theorem pm4_71 (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wb ph (wa ph ps)) $;

--| Implication in terms of biconditional and conjunction. Theorem *4.71 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120 (with conjunct reversed). (Contributed by NM, 25-Jul-1999.)
theorem pm4_71r (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph ps) (wb ph (wa ps ph)) $;

--| Inference converting an implication to a biconditional with conjunction. Inference from Theorem *4.71 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 4-Jan-2004.)
theorem pm4_71i (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wb ph (wa ph ps) $;

--| Inference converting an implication to a biconditional with conjunction. Inference from Theorem *4.71 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120 (with conjunct reversed). (Contributed by NM, 1-Dec-2003.)
theorem pm4_71ri (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wb ph (wa ps ph) $;

--| Deduction converting an implication to a biconditional with conjunction. Deduction from Theorem *4.71 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Dec-2016.)
theorem pm4_71d (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wa ps ch)) $;

--| Deduction converting an implication to a biconditional with conjunction. Deduction from Theorem *4.71 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 120. (Contributed by NM, 10-Feb-2005.)
theorem pm4_71rd (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb ps (wa ch ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.24 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Revised by NM, 14-Mar-2014.)
theorem pm4_24 (ph: wff):
  $ wb ph (wa ph ph) $;

--| Idempotent law for conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 14-Mar-2014.)
theorem anidm (ph: wff):
  $ wb (wa ph ph) ph $;

--| Inference from idempotent law for conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 15-Jun-1994.)
theorem anidms (ph ps: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ph) ps $ >
  $ wi ph ps $;

--| Conjunction idempotence with antecedent. (Contributed by Roy F. Longton, 8-Aug-2005.)
theorem anidmdbi (ph ps: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wa ps ps)) (wi ph ps) $;

--| Associative law for conjunction applied to antecedent (eliminates syllogism). (Contributed by NM, 15-Nov-2002.)
theorem anasss (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $;

--| Associative law for conjunction applied to antecedent (eliminates syllogism). (Contributed by NM, 15-Nov-2002.)
theorem anassrs (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $;

--| Associative law for conjunction. Theorem *4.32 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 118. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Nov-2012.)
theorem anass (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wa (wa ph ps) ch) (wa ph (wa ps ch)) $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 10-Mar-2005.)
theorem sylanl1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ps ch) th) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ch) th) ta $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jan-2005.)
theorem sylanl2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ps ch) th) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ps ph) th) ta $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 9-Apr-2005.)
theorem sylanr1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps (wa ch th)) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa ps (wa ph th)) ta $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 9-Apr-2005.)
theorem sylanr2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi (wa ps (wa ch th)) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa ps (wa ch ph)) ta $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 2-May-1996.)
theorem sylani (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ps (wi (wa ch th) ta) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi (wa ph th) ta) $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1994.)
theorem sylan2i (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ps (wi (wa ch th) ta) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi (wa ch ph) ta) $;

--| A syllogism inference. (Contributed by NM, 3-Aug-1999.)
theorem syl2ani (ph ps ch th ta et: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi et th $ >
  $ wi ps (wi (wa ch th) ta) $ >
  $ wi ps (wi (wa ph et) ta) $;

--| Nested syllogism inference conjoining dissimilar antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem sylan9 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ch ta) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph th) (wi ps ta) $;

--| Nested syllogism inference conjoining dissimilar antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem sylan9r (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wi ch ta) $ >
  $ wi (wa th ph) (wi ps ta) $;

--| Syllogism inference combined with contraction. (Contributed by NM, 16-Mar-2012.)
theorem syl2anc (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Syllogism inference combined with modus ponens. (Contributed by Jeff Madsen, 2-Sep-2009.)
theorem sylancl (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Syllogism inference combined with modus ponens. (Contributed by Jeff Madsen, 2-Sep-2009.)
theorem sylancr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Syllogism inference. (Contributed by Jeff Madsen, 2-Sep-2009.)
theorem sylanbrc (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wb th (wa ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| A syllogism inference combined with contraction. (Contributed by NM, 3-Sep-2004.)
theorem sylancb (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ph ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| A syllogism inference combined with contraction. (Contributed by NM, 3-Sep-2004.)
theorem sylancbr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ps ph $ >
  $ wb ch ph $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| Syllogism inference with commutation of antecents. (Contributed by NM, 2-Jul-2008.)
theorem sylancom (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ch ps) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) th $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 23-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 22-Nov-2012.)
theorem mpdan (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens with commutation of antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 28-Oct-2003.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Apr-2013.)
theorem mpancom (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ps ph $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ps ch $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 30-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Apr-2013.)
theorem mpan (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ps ch $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 16-Sep-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Nov-2012.)
theorem mpan2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi ph ch $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 13-Apr-1995.)
theorem mp2an (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ ch $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by Jeff Madsen, 15-Jun-2011.)
theorem mp4an (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ th $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) (wa ch th)) ta $ >
  $ ta $;

--| A deduction based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 12-Dec-2004.)
theorem mpan2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| A deduction based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 12-Dec-2004.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Apr-2013.)
theorem mpand (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 10-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Nov-2012.)
theorem mpani (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ch th) $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 10-Apr-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 19-Nov-2012.)
theorem mpan2i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 12-Dec-2004.)
theorem mp2ani (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| A deduction based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 12-Dec-2004.)
theorem mp2and (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) th) $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 16-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Apr-2013.)
theorem mpanl1 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ch) th $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 16-Aug-1994.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem mpanl2 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 13-Jul-2005.)
theorem mpanl12 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi ch th $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 3-May-1994.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem mpanr1 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 3-May-1994.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Apr-2013.)
theorem mpanr2 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) th $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 24-Jul-2009.)
theorem mpanr12 (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi ph th $;

--| An inference based on modus ponens. (Contributed by NM, 30-Dec-2004.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 7-Apr-2013.)
theorem mpanlr1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th) ta $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ch) th) ta $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (deduction rule). (Contributed by NM, 4-May-2007.)
theorem pm5_74da (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wi ps ch) (wi ps th)) $;

--| Distribution of implication with conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 31-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 6-Dec-2012.)
theorem imdistan (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wi ps ch)) (wi (wa ph ps) (wa ph ch)) $;

--| Distribution of implication with conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1994.)
theorem imdistani (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wa ph ch) $;

--| Distribution of implication with conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jan-2002.)
theorem imdistanri (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi (wa ps ph) (wa ch ph) $;

--| Distribution of implication with conjunction (deduction rule). (Contributed by NM, 27-Aug-2004.)
theorem imdistand (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) (wa ps th)) $;

--| Distribution of implication with conjunction (deduction version with conjoined antecedent). (Contributed by Jeff Madsen, 19-Jun-2011.)
theorem imdistanda (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wa ps ch) (wa ps th)) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (deduction rule). (Contributed by NM, 29-Oct-1996.) (Revised by NM, 31-Jan-2015.)
theorem pm5_32d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wb ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wa ps ch) (wa ps th)) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (deduction rule). (Contributed by NM, 25-Dec-2004.)
theorem pm5_32rd (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wb ch th)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wa ch ps) (wa th ps)) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (deduction rule). (Contributed by NM, 9-Dec-2006.)
theorem pm5_32da (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) (wb ch th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wa ps ch) (wa ps th)) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional. Theorem *5.32 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1994.) (Revised by NM, 31-Jan-2015.)
theorem pm5_32 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi ph (wb ps ch)) (wb (wa ph ps) (wa ph ch)) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (inference rule). (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1994.)
theorem pm5_32i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wb (wa ph ps) (wa ph ch) $;

--| Distribution of implication over biconditional (inference rule). (Contributed by NM, 12-Mar-1995.)
theorem pm5_32ri (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wb (wa ps ph) (wa ch ph) $;

--| Add a conjunction to an equivalence. (Contributed by Jeff Madsen, 20-Jun-2011.)
theorem biadan2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ps (wb ph ch) $ >
  $ wb ph (wa ps ch) $;

--| Introduce a left conjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 16-Nov-2013.)
theorem anbi2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wa ch ph) (wa ch ps) $;

--| Introduce a right conjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 16-Nov-2013.)
theorem anbi1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wa ph ch) (wa ps ch) $;

--| Variant of ~ anbi2i with commutation. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 14-Jun-2011.)
theorem anbi2ci (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb (wa ph ch) (wa ch ps) $;

--| Conjoin both sides of two equivalences. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem anbi12i (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb (wa ph ch) (wa ps th) $;

--| Variant of ~ anbi12i with commutation. (Contributed by Jonathan Ben-Naim, 3-Jun-2011.)
theorem anbi12ci (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wb ph ps $ >
  $ wb ch th $ >
  $ wb (wa ph ch) (wa th ps) $;

--| Nested syllogism inference conjoining dissimilar antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 4-Mar-1995.)
theorem sylan9bb (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wb ch ta) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph th) (wb ps ta) $;

--| Nested syllogism inference conjoining dissimilar antecedents. (Contributed by NM, 4-Mar-1995.)
theorem sylan9bbr (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi th (wb ch ta) $ >
  $ wi (wa th ph) (wb ps ta) $;

--| Deduction adding a left conjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 16-Nov-2013.)
theorem anbi2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wa th ps) (wa th ch)) $;

--| Deduction adding a right conjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 16-Nov-2013.)
theorem anbi1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wa ps th) (wa ch th)) $;

--| Introduce a right conjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. Theorem *4.36 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 118. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem anbi1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph ps) (wb (wa ph ch) (wa ps ch)) $;

--| Introduce a left conjunct to both sides of a logical equivalence. (Contributed by NM, 16-Nov-2013.)
theorem anbi2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wb ph ps) (wb (wa ch ph) (wa ch ps)) $;

--| Theorem *4.22 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 117. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.)
theorem bitr (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wb ph ps) (wb ps ch)) (wb ph ch) $;

--| Deduction joining two equivalences to form equivalence of conjunctions. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-1993.)
theorem anbi12d (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wb ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb th ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wa ps th) (wa ch ta)) $;

--| Modus ponens mixed with several conjunctions. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 7-Jan-2018.)
theorem mpan10 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wi ph ps) ch) ph) (wa ps ch) $;

--| Theorem *5.3 of [WhiteheadRussell] p. 125. (Contributed by NM, 3-Jan-2005.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem pm5_3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wb (wi (wa ph ps) ch) (wi (wa ph ps) (wa ph ch)) $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 4-May-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Nov-2012.)
theorem adantll (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa th ph) ps) ch $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 4-May-1994.) (Proof shortened by Wolf Lammen, 24-Nov-2012.)
theorem adantlr (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ps) ch $ >
  $ wi (wa (wa ph th) ps) ch $;

