--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem _3adantl1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ta ph ps) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem _3adantl2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ta ps) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem _3adantl3 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa (wa ph ps) ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ps ta) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 27-Apr-2005.)
theorem _3adantr1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ta ps ch)) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 27-Apr-2005.)
theorem _3adantr2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ps ta ch)) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjunct to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 27-Apr-2005.)
theorem _3adantr3 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph (wa ps ch)) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ps ch ta)) th $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2007.)
theorem _3ad2antl1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ph ps ta) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2007.)
theorem _3ad2antl2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ps ph ta) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 4-Aug-2007.)
theorem _3ad2antl3 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa (w3a ps ta ph) ch) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 25-Dec-2007.)
theorem _3ad2antr1 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ch ps ta)) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 27-Dec-2007.)
theorem _3ad2antr2 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ps ch ta)) th $;

--| Deduction adding a conjuncts to antecedent. (Contributed by NM, 30-Dec-2007.)
theorem _3ad2antr3 (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (wa ph ch) th $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (w3a ps ta ch)) th $;

--| Remove a hypothesis from the second member of a biimplication. (Contributed by FL, 22-Jul-2008.)
theorem _3anibar (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) (wb th (wa ch ta)) $ >
  $ wi (w3a ph ps ch) (wb th ta) $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Apr-1995.)
theorem _3mix1 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (w3o ph ps ch) $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Apr-1995.)
theorem _3mix2 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (w3o ps ph ch) $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Apr-1995.)
theorem _3mix3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (w3o ps ch ph) $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Oct-2014.)
theorem _3mix1i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ w3o ph ps ch $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Oct-2014.)
theorem _3mix2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ w3o ps ph ch $;

--| Introduction in triple disjunction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Oct-2014.)
theorem _3mix3i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ w3o ps ch ph $;

--| Deduction introducing triple disjunction. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 8-Jun-2011.)
theorem _3mix1d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (w3o ps ch th) $;

--| Deduction introducing triple disjunction. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 8-Jun-2011.)
theorem _3mix2d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (w3o ch ps th) $;

--| Deduction introducing triple disjunction. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 8-Jun-2011.)
theorem _3mix3d (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph (w3o ch th ps) $;

--| Infer conjunction of premises. (Contributed by NM, 10-Feb-1995.)
theorem _3pm3_2i (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ ph $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ w3a ph ps ch $;

--| ~ pm3.2 for a triple conjunction. (Contributed by Alan Sare, 24-Oct-2011.)
theorem pm3_2an3 (ph ps ch: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps (wi ch (w3a ph ps ch))) $;

--| Join consequents with conjunction. (Contributed by NM, 9-Apr-1994.)
theorem _3jca (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ wi ph ps $ >
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
  $ wi ph (w3a ps ch th) $;

--| Deduction conjoining the consequents of three implications. (Contributed by NM, 25-Sep-2005.)
theorem _3jcad (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph (wi ps ch) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps th) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps ta) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi ps (w3a ch th ta)) $;

--| Detach a conjunction of truths in a biconditional. (Contributed by NM, 16-Sep-2011.) (Revised by NM, 9-Jan-2015.)
theorem mpbir3an (ph ps ch th: wff):
  $ ps $ >
  $ ch $ >
  $ th $ >
  $ wb ph (w3a ps ch th) $ >
  $ ph $;

--| Detach a conjunction of truths in a biconditional. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 11-May-2014.)
theorem mpbir3and (ph ps ch th ta: wff):
  $ wi ph ch $ >
  $ wi ph th $ >
