--| Lemma for ~ cauappcvgpr . Part of showing the putative limit to be a limit. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Jun-2020.)
theorem cauappcvgprlem1 {u q p l: setvar} (ph: wff u l) (A2: class u q l) (Q R F: class) (L: class u l):
  $ wi ph (wf cnq cnq F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral p (wral q (wa (wbr (cfv (cv p) F) (co (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cv p) (cv q) cplq) cplq) cltq) (wbr (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cfv (cv p) F) (co (cv p) (cv q) cplq) cplq) cltq)) cnq) cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral p (wbr A2 (cfv (cv p) F) cltq) cnq) $ >
  $ wceq L (cop (crab l (wrex q (wbr (co (cv l) (cv q) cplq) (cfv (cv q) F) cltq) cnq) cnq) (crab u (wrex q (wbr (co (cfv (cv q) F) (cv q) cplq) (cv u) cltq) cnq) cnq)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Q cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv Q F) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv Q F) (cv u) cltq))) (co L (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (co Q R cplq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (co Q R cplq) (cv u) cltq))) cpp) cltp) $;

--| Lemma for ~ cauappcvgpr . Part of showing the putative limit to be a limit. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Jun-2020.)
theorem cauappcvgprlem2 {u q p l: setvar} (ph: wff u l) (A2: class u q l) (Q R F: class) (L: class u l):
  $ wi ph (wf cnq cnq F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral p (wral q (wa (wbr (cfv (cv p) F) (co (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cv p) (cv q) cplq) cplq) cltq) (wbr (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cfv (cv p) F) (co (cv p) (cv q) cplq) cplq) cltq)) cnq) cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral p (wbr A2 (cfv (cv p) F) cltq) cnq) $ >
  $ wceq L (cop (crab l (wrex q (wbr (co (cv l) (cv q) cplq) (cfv (cv q) F) cltq) cnq) cnq) (crab u (wrex q (wbr (co (cfv (cv q) F) (cv q) cplq) (cv u) cltq) cnq) cnq)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel Q cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel R cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr L (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (co (cfv Q F) (co Q R cplq) cplq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (co (cfv Q F) (co Q R cplq) cplq) (cv u) cltq))) cltp) $;

--| Lemma for ~ cauappcvgpr . The putative limit is a limit. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 20-Jun-2020.)
theorem cauappcvgprlemlim {u r q p l: setvar} (ph: wff u r l) (A2: class u r q l) (F: class) (L: class u l):
  $ wi ph (wf cnq cnq F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral p (wral q (wa (wbr (cfv (cv p) F) (co (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cv p) (cv q) cplq) cplq) cltq) (wbr (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cfv (cv p) F) (co (cv p) (cv q) cplq) cplq) cltq)) cnq) cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral p (wbr A2 (cfv (cv p) F) cltq) cnq) $ >
  $ wceq L (cop (crab l (wrex q (wbr (co (cv l) (cv q) cplq) (cfv (cv q) F) cltq) cnq) cnq) (crab u (wrex q (wbr (co (cfv (cv q) F) (cv q) cplq) (cv u) cltq) cnq) cnq)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral q (wral r (wa (wbr (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cv q) F) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cv q) F) (cv u) cltq))) (co L (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (co (cv q) (cv r) cplq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (co (cv q) (cv r) cplq) (cv u) cltq))) cpp) cltp) (wbr L (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (co (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cv q) (cv r) cplq) cplq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (co (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cv q) (cv r) cplq) cplq) (cv u) cltq))) cltp)) cnq) cnq) $;

--| A Cauchy approximation has a limit. A Cauchy approximation, here ` F ` , is similar to a Cauchy sequence but is indexed by the desired tolerance (that is, how close together terms needs to be) rather than by natural numbers. This is basically Theorem 11.2.12 of [HoTT], p. (varies) with a few differences such as that we are proving the existence of a limit without anything about how fast it converges (that is, mere existence instead of existence, in HoTT terms), and that the codomain of ` F ` is ` Q. ` rather than ` P. ` . We also specify that every term needs to be larger than a fraction ` A ` , to avoid the case where we have positive terms which "converge" to zero (which is not a positive real). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Jun-2020.)
theorem cauappcvgpr {y1 u r q p l: setvar} (ph: wff y1 u r l) (A2: class y1 u r q l) (F: class):
  $ wi ph (wf cnq cnq F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral p (wral q (wa (wbr (cfv (cv p) F) (co (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cv p) (cv q) cplq) cplq) cltq) (wbr (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cfv (cv p) F) (co (cv p) (cv q) cplq) cplq) cltq)) cnq) cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral p (wbr A2 (cfv (cv p) F) cltq) cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrex y1 (wral q (wral r (wa (wbr (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cv q) F) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cv q) F) (cv u) cltq))) (co (cv y1) (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (co (cv q) (cv r) cplq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (co (cv q) (cv r) cplq) (cv u) cltq))) cpp) cltp) (wbr (cv y1) (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (co (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cv q) (cv r) cplq) cplq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (co (cfv (cv q) F) (co (cv q) (cv r) cplq) cplq) (cv u) cltq))) cltp)) cnq) cnq) cnp) $;

--| Archimedean principle for fractions (reciprocal version). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Sep-2020.)
theorem archrecnq {j: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnq) (wrex j (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv j) c1o) ceq) crq) A2 cltq) cnpi) $;

--| Archimedean principle for positive reals (reciprocal version). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Nov-2020.)
theorem archrecpr {u j l: setvar} (A2: class u l):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnp) (wrex j (wbr (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv j) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv j) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) A2 cltp) cnpi) $;

--| Lemma for ~ caucvgpr . Reciprocals of positive integers decrease as the positive integers increase. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Oct-2020.)
theorem caucvgprlemk (ph: wff) (Q J K: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr J K clti) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cfv (cec (cop J c1o) ceq) crq) Q cltq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (cfv (cec (cop K c1o) ceq) crq) Q cltq) $;

--| Lemma for ~ caucvgpr . Part of disjointness. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Oct-2020.)
theorem caucvgprlemnkj {k n: setvar} (ph: wff k n) (S: class k n) (F: class) (J K: class k n):
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnq F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wral k (wi (wbr (cv n) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv n) F) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) cltq) (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co (cfv (cv n) F) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) cltq))) cnpi) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel K cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel J cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel S cnq) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wa (wbr (co S (cfv (cec (cop K c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) (cfv K F) cltq) (wbr (co (cfv J F) (cfv (cec (cop J c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) S cltq))) $;

--| Lemma for ~ caucvgpr . Non-existence of two elements of the sequence which are too far from each other. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 18-Oct-2020.)
theorem caucvgprlemnbj {k n: setvar} (ph: wff k n) (B2 F J: class):
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnq F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wral k (wi (wbr (cv n) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv n) F) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) cltq) (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co (cfv (cv n) F) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) cltq))) cnpi) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel J cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wn (wbr (co (co (cfv B2 F) (cfv (cec (cop B2 c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) (cfv (cec (cop J c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) (cfv J F) cltq)) $;

