--| Lemma for ~ caucvgprpr . The putative limit is a limit. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Nov-2020.)
theorem caucvgprprlemlim {x3 u j k m n r q p l: setvar} (ph: wff u m n q p l) (A2: class x3 u k n q p l) (F: class x3 j q p) (L: class x3 u j m n r q p l):
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnp F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wral k (wi (wbr (cv n) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv n) F) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) cpp) cltp) (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co (cfv (cv n) F) (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) cpp) cltp))) cnpi) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral m (wbr A2 (cfv (cv m) F) cltp) cnpi) $ >
  $ wceq L (cop (crab l (wrex r (wbr (cop (cab p (wbr (cv p) (co (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv r) c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) cltq)) (cab q (wbr (co (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv r) c1o) ceq) crq) cplq) (cv q) cltq))) (cfv (cv r) F) cltp) cnpi) cnq) (crab u (wrex r (wbr (co (cfv (cv r) F) (cop (cab p (wbr (cv p) (cfv (cec (cop (cv r) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab q (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv r) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv q) cltq))) cpp) (cop (cab p (wbr (cv p) (cv u) cltq)) (cab q (wbr (cv u) (cv q) cltq))) cltp) cnpi) cnq)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral x3 (wrex j (wral k (wi (wbr (cv j) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co L (cv x3) cpp) cltp) (wbr L (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cv x3) cpp) cltp))) cnpi) cnpi) cnp) $;

--| A Cauchy sequence of positive reals with a modulus of convergence converges to a positive real. This is basically Corollary 11.2.13 of [HoTT], p. (varies) (one key difference being that this is for positive reals rather than signed reals). Also, the HoTT book theorem has a modulus of convergence (that is, a rate of convergence) specified by (11.2.9) in HoTT whereas this theorem fixes the rate of convergence to say that all terms after the nth term must be within ` 1 / n ` of the nth term (it should later be able to prove versions of this theorem with a different fixed rate or a modulus of convergence supplied as a hypothesis). We also specify that every term needs to be larger than a given value ` A ` , to avoid the case where we have positive terms which "converge" to zero (which is not a positive real). This is similar to ~ caucvgpr except that values of the sequence are positive reals rather than positive fractions. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 14-Nov-2020.)
theorem caucvgprpr {x3 y1 u j k m n l: setvar} (ph: wff y1 u m n l) (A2: class x3 y1 u k n l) (F: class):
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnp F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wral k (wi (wbr (cv n) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv n) F) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) cpp) cltp) (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co (cfv (cv n) F) (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) cpp) cltp))) cnpi) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral m (wbr A2 (cfv (cv m) F) cltp) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wrex y1 (wral x3 (wrex j (wral k (wi (wbr (cv j) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co (cv y1) (cv x3) cpp) cltp) (wbr (cv y1) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cv x3) cpp) cltp))) cnpi) cnpi) cnp) cnp) $;

--| Define equivalence relation for signed reals. This is a "temporary" set used in the construction of complex numbers, and is intended to be used only by the construction. From Proposition 9-4.1 of [Gleason] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 25-Jul-1995.)
axiom df_enr {x3 y1 z w v u: setvar}:
  $ wceq cer (copab x3 y1 (wa (wa (wcel (cv x3) (cxp cnp cnp)) (wcel (cv y1) (cxp cnp cnp))) (wex z (wex w (wex v (wex u (wa (wa (wceq (cv x3) (cop (cv z) (cv w))) (wceq (cv y1) (cop (cv v) (cv u)))) (wceq (co (cv z) (cv u) cpp) (co (cv w) (cv v) cpp))))))))) $;

--| Define class of signed reals. This is a "temporary" set used in the construction of complex numbers, and is intended to be used only by the construction. From Proposition 9-4.2 of [Gleason] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 25-Jul-1995.)
axiom df_nr:
  $ wceq cnr (cqs (cxp cnp cnp) cer) $;

--| Define addition on signed reals. This is a "temporary" set used in the construction of complex numbers, and is intended to be used only by the construction. From Proposition 9-4.3 of [Gleason] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 25-Aug-1995.)
axiom df_plr {x3 y1 z w v u f2: setvar}:
  $ wceq cplr (coprab x3 y1 z (wa (wa (wcel (cv x3) cnr) (wcel (cv y1) cnr)) (wex w (wex v (wex u (wex f2 (wa (wa (wceq (cv x3) (cec (cop (cv w) (cv v)) cer)) (wceq (cv y1) (cec (cop (cv u) (cv f2)) cer))) (wceq (cv z) (cec (cop (co (cv w) (cv u) cpp) (co (cv v) (cv f2) cpp)) cer))))))))) $;

--| Define multiplication on signed reals. This is a "temporary" set used in the construction of complex numbers, and is intended to be used only by the construction. From Proposition 9-4.3 of [Gleason] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 25-Aug-1995.)
axiom df_mr {x3 y1 z w v u f2: setvar}:
  $ wceq cmr (coprab x3 y1 z (wa (wa (wcel (cv x3) cnr) (wcel (cv y1) cnr)) (wex w (wex v (wex u (wex f2 (wa (wa (wceq (cv x3) (cec (cop (cv w) (cv v)) cer)) (wceq (cv y1) (cec (cop (cv u) (cv f2)) cer))) (wceq (cv z) (cec (cop (co (co (cv w) (cv u) cmp) (co (cv v) (cv f2) cmp) cpp) (co (co (cv w) (cv f2) cmp) (co (cv v) (cv u) cmp) cpp)) cer))))))))) $;

--| Define ordering relation on signed reals. This is a "temporary" set used in the construction of complex numbers, and is intended to be used only by the construction. From Proposition 9-4.4 of [Gleason] p. 127. (Contributed by NM, 14-Feb-1996.)
axiom df_ltr {x3 y1 z w v u: setvar}:
  $ wceq cltr (copab x3 y1 (wa (wa (wcel (cv x3) cnr) (wcel (cv y1) cnr)) (wex z (wex w (wex v (wex u (wa (wa (wceq (cv x3) (cec (cop (cv z) (cv w)) cer)) (wceq (cv y1) (cec (cop (cv v) (cv u)) cer))) (wbr (co (cv z) (cv u) cpp) (co (cv w) (cv v) cpp) cltp)))))))) $;

--| Define signed real constant 0. This is a "temporary" set used in the construction of complex numbers, and is intended to be used only by the construction. From Proposition 9-4.2 of [Gleason] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 9-Aug-1995.)
axiom df_0r:
  $ wceq c0r (cec (cop c1p c1p) cer) $;

--| Define signed real constant 1. This is a "temporary" set used in the construction of complex numbers, and is intended to be used only by the construction. From Proposition 9-4.2 of [Gleason] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 9-Aug-1995.)
axiom df_1r:
  $ wceq c1r (cec (cop (co c1p c1p cpp) c1p) cer) $;

--| Define signed real constant -1. This is a "temporary" set used in the construction of complex numbers, and is intended to be used only by the construction. (Contributed by NM, 9-Aug-1995.)
axiom df_m1r:
  $ wceq cm1r (cec (cop c1p (co c1p c1p cpp)) cer) $;

--| Equivalence relation for signed reals in terms of positive reals. (Contributed by NM, 3-Sep-1995.)
theorem enrbreq (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wa (wcel C cnp) (wcel D cnp))) (wb (wbr (cop A2 B2) (cop C D) cer) (wceq (co A2 D cpp) (co B2 C cpp))) $;

--| The equivalence relation for signed reals is an equivalence relation. Proposition 9-4.1 of [Gleason] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 3-Sep-1995.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 6-Jul-2015.)
theorem enrer:
  $ wer (cxp cnp cnp) cer $;

--| Equivalence class equality of positive fractions in terms of positive integers. (Contributed by NM, 29-Nov-1995.)
theorem enreceq (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wa (wcel C cnp) (wcel D cnp))) (wb (wceq (cec (cop A2 B2) cer) (cec (cop C D) cer)) (wceq (co A2 D cpp) (co B2 C cpp))) $;

--| The equivalence relation for signed reals exists. (Contributed by NM, 25-Jul-1995.)
theorem enrex:
  $ wcel cer cvv $;

--| Signed real 'less than' is a relation on signed reals. (Contributed by NM, 14-Feb-1996.)
theorem ltrelsr:
  $ wss cltr (cxp cnr cnr) $;

--| Lemma showing compatibility of addition. (Contributed by NM, 3-Sep-1995.)
theorem addcmpblnr (A2 B2 C D R S F G: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wa (wcel C cnp) (wcel D cnp))) (wa (wa (wcel F cnp) (wcel G cnp)) (wa (wcel R cnp) (wcel S cnp)))) (wi (wa (wceq (co A2 D cpp) (co B2 C cpp)) (wceq (co F S cpp) (co G R cpp))) (wbr (cop (co A2 F cpp) (co B2 G cpp)) (cop (co C R cpp) (co D S cpp)) cer)) $;

--| Lemma used in lemma showing compatibility of multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 1-Jan-2020.)
theorem mulcmpblnrlemg (A2 B2 C D R S F G: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wa (wcel C cnp) (wcel D cnp))) (wa (wa (wcel F cnp) (wcel G cnp)) (wa (wcel R cnp) (wcel S cnp)))) (wi (wa (wceq (co A2 D cpp) (co B2 C cpp)) (wceq (co F S cpp) (co G R cpp))) (wceq (co (co D F cmp) (co (co (co A2 F cmp) (co B2 G cmp) cpp) (co (co C S cmp) (co D R cmp) cpp) cpp) cpp) (co (co D F cmp) (co (co (co A2 G cmp) (co B2 F cmp) cpp) (co (co C R cmp) (co D S cmp) cpp) cpp) cpp))) $;

--| Lemma showing compatibility of multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 5-Sep-1995.)
theorem mulcmpblnr (A2 B2 C D R S F G: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wa (wcel C cnp) (wcel D cnp))) (wa (wa (wcel F cnp) (wcel G cnp)) (wa (wcel R cnp) (wcel S cnp)))) (wi (wa (wceq (co A2 D cpp) (co B2 C cpp)) (wceq (co F S cpp) (co G R cpp))) (wbr (cop (co (co A2 F cmp) (co B2 G cmp) cpp) (co (co A2 G cmp) (co B2 F cmp) cpp)) (cop (co (co C R cmp) (co D S cmp) cpp) (co (co C S cmp) (co D R cmp) cpp)) cer)) $;

--| Decomposing signed reals into positive reals. Lemma for ~ addsrpr and ~ mulsrpr . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 30-Dec-2019.)
theorem prsrlem1 (w v u t: setvar) (A2 B2: class) (f2 g1 h s1: setvar):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 (cqs (cxp cnp cnp) cer)) (wcel B2 (cqs (cxp cnp cnp) cer))) (wa (wa (wceq A2 (cec (cop (cv w) (cv v)) cer)) (wceq B2 (cec (cop (cv u) (cv t)) cer))) (wa (wceq A2 (cec (cop (cv s1) (cv f2)) cer)) (wceq B2 (cec (cop (cv g1) (cv h)) cer))))) (wa (wa (wa (wa (wcel (cv w) cnp) (wcel (cv v) cnp)) (wa (wcel (cv s1) cnp) (wcel (cv f2) cnp))) (wa (wa (wcel (cv u) cnp) (wcel (cv t) cnp)) (wa (wcel (cv g1) cnp) (wcel (cv h) cnp)))) (wa (wceq (co (cv w) (cv f2) cpp) (co (cv v) (cv s1) cpp)) (wceq (co (cv u) (cv h) cpp) (co (cv t) (cv g1) cpp)))) $;

--| There is at most one result from adding signed reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 30-Dec-2019.)
theorem addsrmo {z w v u t: setvar} (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 (cqs (cxp cnp cnp) cer)) (wcel B2 (cqs (cxp cnp cnp) cer))) (wmo z (wex w (wex v (wex u (wex t (wa (wa (wceq A2 (cec (cop (cv w) (cv v)) cer)) (wceq B2 (cec (cop (cv u) (cv t)) cer))) (wceq (cv z) (cec (cop (co (cv w) (cv u) cpp) (co (cv v) (cv t) cpp)) cer)))))))) $;

--| There is at most one result from multiplying signed reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 30-Dec-2019.)
theorem mulsrmo {z w v u t: setvar} (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 (cqs (cxp cnp cnp) cer)) (wcel B2 (cqs (cxp cnp cnp) cer))) (wmo z (wex w (wex v (wex u (wex t (wa (wa (wceq A2 (cec (cop (cv w) (cv v)) cer)) (wceq B2 (cec (cop (cv u) (cv t)) cer))) (wceq (cv z) (cec (cop (co (co (cv w) (cv u) cmp) (co (cv v) (cv t) cmp) cpp) (co (co (cv w) (cv t) cmp) (co (cv v) (cv u) cmp) cpp)) cer)))))))) $;

--| Addition of signed reals in terms of positive reals. (Contributed by NM, 3-Sep-1995.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 12-Aug-2015.)
theorem addsrpr (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wa (wcel C cnp) (wcel D cnp))) (wceq (co (cec (cop A2 B2) cer) (cec (cop C D) cer) cplr) (cec (cop (co A2 C cpp) (co B2 D cpp)) cer)) $;

--| Multiplication of signed reals in terms of positive reals. (Contributed by NM, 3-Sep-1995.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 12-Aug-2015.)
theorem mulsrpr (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wa (wcel C cnp) (wcel D cnp))) (wceq (co (cec (cop A2 B2) cer) (cec (cop C D) cer) cmr) (cec (cop (co (co A2 C cmp) (co B2 D cmp) cpp) (co (co A2 D cmp) (co B2 C cmp) cpp)) cer)) $;

--| Ordering of signed reals in terms of positive reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Jan-2019.)
theorem ltsrprg (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wa (wcel C cnp) (wcel D cnp))) (wb (wbr (cec (cop A2 B2) cer) (cec (cop C D) cer) cltr) (wbr (co A2 D cpp) (co B2 C cpp) cltp)) $;

--| Greater than zero in terms of positive reals. (Contributed by NM, 13-May-1996.)
theorem gt0srpr (A2 B2: class):
  $ wb (wbr c0r (cec (cop A2 B2) cer) cltr) (wbr B2 A2 cltp) $;

--| The empty set is not a signed real. (Contributed by NM, 25-Aug-1995.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 10-Jul-2014.)
theorem _0nsr:
  $ wn (wcel c0 cnr) $;

--| The constant ` 0R ` is a signed real. (Contributed by NM, 9-Aug-1995.)
theorem _0r:
  $ wcel c0r cnr $;

--| The constant ` 1R ` is a signed real. (Contributed by NM, 9-Aug-1995.)
theorem _1sr:
  $ wcel c1r cnr $;

--| The constant ` -1R ` is a signed real. (Contributed by NM, 9-Aug-1995.)
theorem m1r:
  $ wcel cm1r cnr $;

--| Closure of addition on signed reals. (Contributed by NM, 25-Jul-1995.)
theorem addclsr (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr)) (wcel (co A2 B2 cplr) cnr) $;

--| Closure of multiplication on signed reals. (Contributed by NM, 10-Aug-1995.)
theorem mulclsr (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr)) (wcel (co A2 B2 cmr) cnr) $;

--| Addition of signed reals is commutative. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Jan-2020.)
theorem addcomsrg (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr)) (wceq (co A2 B2 cplr) (co B2 A2 cplr)) $;

--| Addition of signed reals is associative. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Jan-2020.)
theorem addasssrg (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr) (wcel C cnr)) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cplr) C cplr) (co A2 (co B2 C cplr) cplr)) $;

--| Multiplication of signed reals is commutative. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Jan-2020.)
theorem mulcomsrg (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr)) (wceq (co A2 B2 cmr) (co B2 A2 cmr)) $;

--| Multiplication of signed reals is associative. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Jan-2020.)
theorem mulasssrg (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr) (wcel C cnr)) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmr) C cmr) (co A2 (co B2 C cmr) cmr)) $;

--| Multiplication of signed reals is distributive. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 4-Jan-2020.)
theorem distrsrg (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr) (wcel C cnr)) (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cplr) cmr) (co (co A2 B2 cmr) (co A2 C cmr) cplr)) $;

--| Minus one plus one is zero for signed reals. (Contributed by NM, 5-May-1996.)
theorem m1p1sr:
  $ wceq (co cm1r c1r cplr) c0r $;

--| Minus one times minus one is plus one for signed reals. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1996.)
theorem m1m1sr:
  $ wceq (co cm1r cm1r cmr) c1r $;

--| Signed real 'less than' is a transitive relation. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 4-Jan-2019.)
theorem lttrsr (f2 g1 h: setvar):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel (cv f2) cnr) (wcel (cv g1) cnr) (wcel (cv h) cnr)) (wi (wa (wbr (cv f2) (cv g1) cltr) (wbr (cv g1) (cv h) cltr)) (wbr (cv f2) (cv h) cltr)) $;

--| Signed real 'less than' is a partial order. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 4-Jan-2019.)
theorem ltposr:
  $ wpo cnr cltr $;

--| Signed real 'less than' is a strict ordering. (Contributed by NM, 19-Feb-1996.)
theorem ltsosr:
  $ wor cnr cltr $;

--| 0 is less than 1 for signed reals. (Contributed by NM, 26-Mar-1996.)
theorem _0lt1sr:
  $ wbr c0r c1r cltr $;

--| 1 and 0 are distinct for signed reals. (Contributed by NM, 26-Mar-1996.)
theorem _1ne0sr:
  $ wn (wceq c1r c0r) $;

--| The signed real number 0 is an identity element for addition of signed reals. (Contributed by NM, 10-Apr-1996.)
theorem _0idsr (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnr) (wceq (co A2 c0r cplr) A2) $;

--| 1 is an identity element for multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 5-Jan-2020.)
theorem _1idsr (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnr) (wceq (co A2 c1r cmr) A2) $;

--| A signed real times 0 is 0. (Contributed by NM, 10-Apr-1996.)
theorem _00sr (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnr) (wceq (co A2 c0r cmr) c0r) $;

--| Ordering property of addition. (Contributed by NM, 10-May-1996.)
theorem ltasrg (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr) (wcel C cnr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cltr) (wbr (co C A2 cplr) (co C B2 cplr) cltr)) $;

--| A signed real plus its negative is zero. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1996.)
theorem pn0sr (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnr) (wceq (co A2 (co A2 cm1r cmr) cplr) c0r) $;

--| Existence of negative signed real. Part of Proposition 9-4.3 of [Gleason] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 2-May-1996.)
theorem negexsr {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnr) (wrex x3 (wceq (co A2 (cv x3) cplr) c0r) cnr) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive signed real exists and is positive. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 6-Feb-2020.)
theorem recexgt0sr {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wbr c0r A2 cltr) (wrex x3 (wa (wbr c0r (cv x3) cltr) (wceq (co A2 (cv x3) cmr) c1r)) cnr) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive signed real exists. Part of Proposition 9-4.3 of [Gleason] p. 126. (Contributed by NM, 15-May-1996.)
theorem recexsrlem {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wbr c0r A2 cltr) (wrex x3 (wceq (co A2 (cv x3) cmr) c1r) cnr) $;

--| The sum of two positive signed reals is positive. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1996.)
theorem addgt0sr (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wbr c0r A2 cltr) (wbr c0r B2 cltr)) (wbr c0r (co A2 B2 cplr) cltr) $;

--| Adding one to a signed real yields a larger signed real. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 7-Jul-2021.)
theorem ltadd1sr (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnr) (wbr A2 (co A2 c1r cplr) cltr) $;

--| The product of two positive signed reals is positive. (Contributed by NM, 13-May-1996.)
theorem mulgt0sr (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wbr c0r A2 cltr) (wbr c0r B2 cltr)) (wbr c0r (co A2 B2 cmr) cltr) $;

--| Apartness of signed reals is tight. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Jan-2020.)
theorem aptisr (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr) (wn (wo (wbr A2 B2 cltr) (wbr B2 A2 cltr)))) (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Lemma for ~ mulextsr1 . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 17-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulextsr1lem (U V W X Y Z: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel X cnp) (wcel Y cnp)) (wa (wcel Z cnp) (wcel W cnp)) (wa (wcel U cnp) (wcel V cnp))) (wi (wbr (co (co (co X U cmp) (co Y V cmp) cpp) (co (co Z V cmp) (co W U cmp) cpp) cpp) (co (co (co X V cmp) (co Y U cmp) cpp) (co (co Z U cmp) (co W V cmp) cpp) cpp) cltp) (wo (wbr (co X W cpp) (co Y Z cpp) cltp) (wbr (co Z Y cpp) (co W X cpp) cltp))) $;

--| Strong extensionality of multiplication of signed reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 18-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulextsr1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cnr) (wcel B2 cnr) (wcel C cnr)) (wi (wbr (co A2 C cmr) (co B2 C cmr) cltr) (wo (wbr A2 B2 cltr) (wbr B2 A2 cltr))) $;

--| For any signed real, there is an integer that is greater than it. This is also known as the "archimedean property". The expression ` [ <. ( <. { l | l <Q [ <. x , 1o >. ] ~Q } ` , ` { u | [ <. x , 1o >. ] ~Q <Q u } >. +P. 1P ) , 1P >. ] ~R ` is the embedding of the positive integer ` x ` into the signed reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Apr-2020.)
theorem archsr {x3 u l: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnr) (wrex x3 (wbr A2 (cec (cop (co (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cec (cop (cv x3) c1o) ceq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cec (cop (cv x3) c1o) ceq) (cv u) cltq))) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cltr) cnpi) $;

--| Mapping from a signed real greater than zero to a positive real. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Jun-2021.)
theorem srpospr {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cnr) (wbr c0r A2 cltr)) (wreu x3 (wceq (cec (cop (co (cv x3) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) A2) cnp) $;

--| Mapping from a positive real to a signed real. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Jun-2021.)
theorem prsrcl (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel (cec (cop (co A2 c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cnr) $;

--| Mapping from a positive real to a signed real yields a result greater than zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Jun-2021.)
theorem prsrpos (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cnp) (wbr c0r (cec (cop (co A2 c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cltr) $;

--| Mapping from positive real addition to signed real addition. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Jun-2021.)
theorem prsradd (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wceq (cec (cop (co (co A2 B2 cpp) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) (co (cec (cop (co A2 c1p cpp) c1p) cer) (cec (cop (co B2 c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cplr)) $;

--| Mapping from positive real ordering to signed real ordering. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Jun-2021.)
theorem prsrlt (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cnp) (wcel B2 cnp)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cltp) (wbr (cec (cop (co A2 c1p cpp) c1p) cer) (cec (cop (co B2 c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cltr)) $;

--| Mapping a restricted iota from a positive real to a signed real. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Jun-2021.)
theorem prsrriota {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cnr) (wbr c0r A2 cltr)) (wceq (cec (cop (co (crio x3 (wceq (cec (cop (co (cv x3) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) A2) cnp) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) A2) $;

--| Lemma for ~ caucvgsr . Terms of the sequence from ~ caucvgsrlemgt1 can be mapped to positive reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Jul-2021.)
theorem caucvgsrlemcl {y1 m: setvar} (ph: wff y1 m) (A2 F: class):
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnr F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral m (wbr c1r (cfv (cv m) F) cltr) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel A2 cnpi)) (wcel (crio y1 (wceq (cfv A2 F) (cec (cop (co (cv y1) c1p cpp) c1p) cer)) cnp) cnp) $;

--| Lemma for ~ caucvgsr . The lower bound is a signed real. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 4-Jul-2021.)
theorem caucvgsrlemasr {m: setvar} (ph: wff m) (A2: class) (F: class m):
  $ wi ph (wral m (wbr A2 (cfv (cv m) F) cltr) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cnr) $;

--| Lemma for ~ caucvgsr . Coercing sequence value from a positive real to a signed real. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Jun-2021.)
theorem caucvgsrlemfv {x3 y1 u k m n l: setvar} (ph: wff y1 u k m n l) (A2 F: class u k n l) (G: class x3 y1 u k m n l):
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnr F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wral k (wi (wbr (cv n) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv n) F) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cec (cop (co (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cplr) cltr) (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co (cfv (cv n) F) (cec (cop (co (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cplr) cltr))) cnpi) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral m (wbr c1r (cfv (cv m) F) cltr) cnpi) $ >
  $ wceq G (cmpt x3 cnpi (crio y1 (wceq (cfv (cv x3) F) (cec (cop (co (cv y1) c1p cpp) c1p) cer)) cnp)) $ >
  $ wi (wa ph (wcel A2 cnpi)) (wceq (cec (cop (co (cfv A2 G) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) (cfv A2 F)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ caucvgsr . Defining the sequence in terms of positive reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Jun-2021.)
theorem caucvgsrlemf {x3 y1 u k m n l: setvar} (ph: wff y1 u k m n l) (F: class x3 u k n l) (G: class x3 y1 u k m n l):
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnr F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wral k (wi (wbr (cv n) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv n) F) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cec (cop (co (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cplr) cltr) (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co (cfv (cv n) F) (cec (cop (co (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cplr) cltr))) cnpi) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral m (wbr c1r (cfv (cv m) F) cltr) cnpi) $ >
  $ wceq G (cmpt x3 cnpi (crio y1 (wceq (cfv (cv x3) F) (cec (cop (co (cv y1) c1p cpp) c1p) cer)) cnp)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnp G) $;

--| Lemma for ~ caucvgsr . Defining the Cauchy condition in terms of positive reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Jun-2021.)
theorem caucvgsrlemcau {x3 y1 u k m n l: setvar} (ph: wff y1 u m l) (F: class u k n l) (G: class x3 y1 u k m n l):
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnr F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wral k (wi (wbr (cv n) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv n) F) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cec (cop (co (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cplr) cltr) (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co (cfv (cv n) F) (cec (cop (co (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cplr) cltr))) cnpi) cnpi) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral m (wbr c1r (cfv (cv m) F) cltr) cnpi) $ >
  $ wceq G (cmpt x3 cnpi (crio y1 (wceq (cfv (cv x3) F) (cec (cop (co (cv y1) c1p cpp) c1p) cer)) cnp)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wral k (wi (wbr (cv n) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv n) G) (co (cfv (cv k) G) (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) cpp) cltp) (wbr (cfv (cv k) G) (co (cfv (cv n) G) (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) cpp) cltp))) cnpi) cnpi) $;

--| Lemma for ~ caucvgsr . Defining the boundedness condition in terms of positive reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Jun-2021.)
theorem caucvgsrlembound {x3 y1 u k m n l: setvar} (ph: wff y1 u k m n l) (F: class u k n l) (G: class x3 y1 u k n l):
  $ wi ph (wf cnpi cnr F) $ >
  $ wi ph (wral n (wral k (wi (wbr (cv n) (cv k) clti) (wa (wbr (cfv (cv n) F) (co (cfv (cv k) F) (cec (cop (co (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cplr) cltr) (wbr (cfv (cv k) F) (co (cfv (cv n) F) (cec (cop (co (cop (cab l (wbr (cv l) (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) cltq)) (cab u (wbr (cfv (cec (cop (cv n) c1o) ceq) crq) (cv u) cltq))) c1p cpp) c1p) cer) cplr) cltr))) cnpi) cnpi) $ >
