--| A number is zero iff its negative is zero. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem negeq0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq A2 cc0) (wceq (cneg A2) cc0)) $;

--| A number is nonzero iff its negative is nonzero. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem negne0bd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wne A2 cc0) (wne (cneg A2) cc0)) $;

--| Contraposition law for unary minus. Deduction form of ~ negcon1 . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem negcon1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (cneg A2) B2) (wceq (cneg B2) A2)) $;

--| Contraposition law for unary minus. One-way deduction form of ~ negcon1 . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem negcon1ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cneg A2) B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cneg B2) A2) $;

--| The negatives of two complex numbers are equal iff they are equal. Deduction form of ~ neg11 . Generalization of ~ neg11d . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem neg11ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (cneg A2) (cneg B2)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| If two complex numbers are unequal, so are their negatives. Contrapositive of ~ neg11d . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem negned (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne A2 B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne (cneg A2) (cneg B2)) $;

--| The negative of a nonzero number is nonzero. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem negne0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne A2 cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne (cneg A2) cc0) $;

--| The negative of a real is real. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem negrebd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cneg A2) cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $;

--| Closure law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subcld (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 B2 cmin) cc) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem pncand (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) B2 cmin) A2) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem pncan2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) A2 cmin) B2) $;

--| Subtraction and addition of equals. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem pncan3d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co B2 A2 cmin) caddc) B2) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem npcand (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) B2 caddc) A2) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nncand (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co A2 B2 cmin) cmin) B2) $;

--| Relationship between subtraction and negative. Theorem I.3 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem negsubd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (cneg B2) caddc) (co A2 B2 cmin)) $;

--| Relationship between subtraction and negative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subnegd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (cneg B2) cmin) (co A2 B2 caddc)) $;

--| If the difference between two numbers is zero, they are equal. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subeq0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cmin) cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Two unequal numbers have nonzero difference. See also ~ subap0d which is the same thing for apartness rather than negated equality. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 1-Jan-2017.)
theorem subne0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne A2 B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne (co A2 B2 cmin) cc0) $;

--| The difference of two complex numbers is zero iff they are equal. Deduction form of ~ subeq0 . Generalization of ~ subeq0d . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem subeq0ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cmin) cc0) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| If the difference of two complex numbers is nonzero, they are unequal. Converse of ~ subne0d . Contrapositive of ~ subeq0bd . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem subne0ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne (co A2 B2 cmin) cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne A2 B2) $;

--| If the difference between two numbers is zero, they are equal. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem neg11d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cneg A2) (cneg B2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Distribution of negative over addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem negdid (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cneg (co A2 B2 caddc)) (co (cneg A2) (cneg B2) caddc)) $;

--| Distribution of negative over addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem negdi2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cneg (co A2 B2 caddc)) (co (cneg A2) B2 cmin)) $;

--| Distribution of negative over subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem negsubdid (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cneg (co A2 B2 cmin)) (co (cneg A2) B2 caddc)) $;

--| Distribution of negative over subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem negsubdi2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cneg (co A2 B2 cmin)) (co B2 A2 cmin)) $;

--| Relationship between subtraction and negative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem neg2subd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cneg A2) (cneg B2) cmin) (co B2 A2 cmin)) $;

--| Relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subaddd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cmin) C) (wceq (co B2 C caddc) A2)) $;

--| Relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subadd2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cmin) C) (wceq (co C B2 caddc) A2)) $;

--| Associative-type law for subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem addsubassd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) C cmin) (co A2 (co B2 C cmin) caddc)) $;

--| Law for subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem addsubd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) C cmin) (co (co A2 C cmin) B2 caddc)) $;

--| Commutative/associative law for addition and subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subadd23d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C caddc) (co A2 (co C B2 cmin) caddc)) $;

--| Commutative/associative law for addition and subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem addsub12d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cmin) caddc) (co B2 (co A2 C cmin) caddc)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem npncand (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) (co B2 C cmin) caddc) (co A2 C cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nppcand (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C caddc) B2 caddc) (co A2 C caddc)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nppcan2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 (co B2 C caddc) cmin) C caddc) (co A2 B2 cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nppcan3d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C B2 caddc) caddc) (co A2 C caddc)) $;

--| Law for double subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subsubd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cmin) cmin) (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C caddc)) $;

--| Law for double subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subsub2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cmin) cmin) (co A2 (co C B2 cmin) caddc)) $;

--| Law for double subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subsub3d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cmin) cmin) (co (co A2 C caddc) B2 cmin)) $;

--| Law for double subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subsub4d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C cmin) (co A2 (co B2 C caddc) cmin)) $;

--| Swap the second and third terms in a double subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem sub32d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C cmin) (co (co A2 C cmin) B2 cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnncand (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 (co B2 C cmin) cmin) C cmin) (co A2 B2 cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnncan1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) (co A2 C cmin) cmin) (co C B2 cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnncan2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin) cmin) (co A2 B2 cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem npncan3d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C A2 cmin) caddc) (co C B2 cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for mixed addition and subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem pnpcand (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) (co A2 C caddc) cmin) (co B2 C cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for mixed addition and subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem pnpcan2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) cmin) (co A2 B2 cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for mixed addition and subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem pnncand (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) (co A2 C cmin) cmin) (co B2 C caddc)) $;

--| Cancellation law for mixed addition and subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ppncand (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C B2 cmin) caddc) (co A2 C caddc)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subcand (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cmin) (co A2 C cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 C) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 22-Sep-2016.)
theorem subcan2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. Deduction form of ~ subcan . Generalization of ~ subcand . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem subcanad (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cmin) (co A2 C cmin)) (wceq B2 C)) $;

--| Introducing subtraction on both sides of a statement of inequality. Contrapositive of ~ subcand . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem subneintrd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne B2 C) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne (co A2 B2 cmin) (co A2 C cmin)) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction. Deduction form of ~ subcan2 . Generalization of ~ subcan2d . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem subcan2ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| Introducing subtraction on both sides of a statement of inequality. Contrapositive of ~ subcan2d . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem subneintr2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne A2 B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin)) $;

--| Rearrangement of 4 terms in a mixed addition and subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem addsub4d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) cmin) (co (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 D cmin) caddc)) $;

--| Rearrangement of 4 terms in a mixed addition and subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subadd4d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C D cmin) cmin) (co (co A2 D caddc) (co B2 C caddc) cmin)) $;

--| Rearrangement of 4 terms in a subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem sub4d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C D cmin) cmin) (co (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 D cmin) cmin)) $;

--| Law for subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem _2addsubd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co (co A2 B2 caddc) C caddc) D cmin) (co (co (co A2 C caddc) D cmin) B2 caddc)) $;

--| Relation between sums and differences. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem addsubeq4d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc)) (wceq (co C A2 cmin) (co B2 D cmin))) $;

--| Reverse the order of subtraction in an equality. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 8-Jul-2013.)
theorem subeqrev (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wcel D cc))) (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C D cmin)) (wceq (co B2 A2 cmin) (co D C cmin))) $;

--| Cancellation law for addition and subtraction with 1. (Contributed by Alexander van der Vekens, 3-Oct-2018.)
theorem pncan1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wceq (co (co A2 c1 caddc) c1 cmin) A2) $;

--| Cancellation law for subtraction and addition with 1. (Contributed by Alexander van der Vekens, 5-Oct-2018.)
theorem npcan1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wceq (co (co A2 c1 cmin) c1 caddc) A2) $;

--| If two complex numbers are equal, their difference is zero. Consequence of ~ subeq0ad . Converse of ~ subeq0d . Contrapositive of ~ subne0ad . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem subeq0bd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cmin) cc0) $;

--| Closure law for negative of reals. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem renegcld (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (cneg A2) cr) $;

--| Closure law for subtraction of reals. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem resubcld (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 B2 cmin) cr) $;

--| k times k minus 1 is a complex number if k is a complex number. (Contributed by Alexander van der Vekens, 11-Mar-2018.)
theorem kcnktkm1cn (K: class):
  $ wi (wcel K cc) (wcel (co K (co K c1 cmin) cmul) cc) $;

--| Product of two sums. (Contributed by NM, 14-Jan-2006.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem muladd (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wcel D cc))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) cmul) (co (co (co A2 C cmul) (co D B2 cmul) caddc) (co (co A2 D cmul) (co C B2 cmul) caddc) caddc)) $;

--| Distribution of multiplication over subtraction. Theorem I.5 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 18-Nov-2004.)
theorem subdi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wcel C cc)) (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cmin) cmul) (co (co A2 B2 cmul) (co A2 C cmul) cmin)) $;

--| Distribution of multiplication over subtraction. Theorem I.5 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 30-Dec-2005.)
theorem subdir (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wcel C cc)) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C cmul) (co (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cmin)) $;

--| Multiplication by ` 0 ` . Theorem I.6 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 10-Aug-1999.)
theorem mul02 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wceq (co cc0 A2 cmul) cc0) $;

--| Zero times a real is zero. Although we prove it as a corollary of ~ mul02 , the name is for consistency with the Metamath Proof Explorer which proves it before ~ mul02 . (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 3-Jan-2013.)
theorem mul02lem2 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wceq (co cc0 A2 cmul) cc0) $;

--| Multiplication by ` 0 ` . Theorem I.6 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 15-May-1999.) (Revised by Scott Fenton, 3-Jan-2013.)
theorem mul01 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wceq (co A2 cc0 cmul) cc0) $;

--| Multiplication by 0. Theorem I.6 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 23-Nov-1994.)
theorem mul02i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wceq (co cc0 A2 cmul) cc0 $;

--| Multiplication by ` 0 ` . Theorem I.6 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 23-Nov-1994.) (Revised by Scott Fenton, 3-Jan-2013.)
theorem mul01i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wceq (co A2 cc0 cmul) cc0 $;

--| Multiplication by 0. Theorem I.6 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mul02d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co cc0 A2 cmul) cc0) $;

--| Multiplication by ` 0 ` . Theorem I.6 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mul01d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 cc0 cmul) cc0) $;

--| The imaginary unit ` _i ` is not zero. (Contributed by NM, 6-May-1999.)
theorem ine0:
  $ wne ci cc0 $;

--| Product with negative is negative of product. Theorem I.12 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mulneg1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wceq (co (cneg A2) B2 cmul) (cneg (co A2 B2 cmul))) $;

--| The product with a negative is the negative of the product. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2004.)
theorem mulneg2 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wceq (co A2 (cneg B2) cmul) (cneg (co A2 B2 cmul))) $;

--| Swap the negative sign in a product. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2004.)
theorem mulneg12 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wceq (co (cneg A2) B2 cmul) (co A2 (cneg B2) cmul)) $;

--| Product of two negatives. Theorem I.12 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2004.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem mul2neg (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wceq (co (cneg A2) (cneg B2) cmul) (co A2 B2 cmul)) $;

--| Convert a subtraction to addition using multiplication by a negative. (Contributed by NM, 2-Feb-2007.)
theorem submul2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wcel C cc)) (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cmul) cmin) (co A2 (co B2 (cneg C) cmul) caddc)) $;

--| Product with minus one is negative. (Contributed by NM, 16-Nov-1999.)
theorem mulm1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wceq (co (cneg c1) A2 cmul) (cneg A2)) $;

--| Product of two differences. (Contributed by NM, 14-Jan-2006.)
theorem mulsub (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wcel D cc))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C D cmin) cmul) (co (co (co A2 C cmul) (co D B2 cmul) caddc) (co (co A2 D cmul) (co C B2 cmul) caddc) cmin)) $;

--| Swap the order of subtraction in a multiplication. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 24-Jun-2013.)
theorem mulsub2 (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wcel D cc))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C D cmin) cmul) (co (co B2 A2 cmin) (co D C cmin) cmul)) $;

--| Product with minus one is negative. (Contributed by NM, 31-Jul-1999.)
theorem mulm1i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wceq (co (cneg c1) A2 cmul) (cneg A2) $;

--| Product with negative is negative of product. Theorem I.12 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 10-Feb-1995.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mulneg1i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wceq (co (cneg A2) B2 cmul) (cneg (co A2 B2 cmul)) $;

--| Product with negative is negative of product. (Contributed by NM, 31-Jul-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mulneg2i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wceq (co A2 (cneg B2) cmul) (cneg (co A2 B2 cmul)) $;

--| Product of two negatives. Theorem I.12 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 14-Feb-1995.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mul2negi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wceq (co (cneg A2) (cneg B2) cmul) (co A2 B2 cmul) $;

--| Distribution of multiplication over subtraction. Theorem I.5 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 26-Nov-1994.)
theorem subdii (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cmin) cmul) (co (co A2 B2 cmul) (co A2 C cmul) cmin) $;

--| Distribution of multiplication over subtraction. Theorem I.5 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 8-May-1999.)
theorem subdiri (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C cmul) (co (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cmin) $;

--| Product of two sums. (Contributed by NM, 17-May-1999.)
theorem muladdi (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wcel D cc $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) cmul) (co (co (co A2 C cmul) (co D B2 cmul) caddc) (co (co A2 D cmul) (co C B2 cmul) caddc) caddc) $;

--| Product with minus one is negative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mulm1d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cneg c1) A2 cmul) (cneg A2)) $;

--| Product with negative is negative of product. Theorem I.12 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mulneg1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cneg A2) B2 cmul) (cneg (co A2 B2 cmul))) $;

--| Product with negative is negative of product. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mulneg2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (cneg B2) cmul) (cneg (co A2 B2 cmul))) $;

--| Product of two negatives. Theorem I.12 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mul2negd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cneg A2) (cneg B2) cmul) (co A2 B2 cmul)) $;

--| Distribution of multiplication over subtraction. Theorem I.5 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subdid (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cmin) cmul) (co (co A2 B2 cmul) (co A2 C cmul) cmin)) $;

--| Distribution of multiplication over subtraction. Theorem I.5 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subdird (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C cmul) (co (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cmin)) $;

--| Product of two sums. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem muladdd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) cmul) (co (co (co A2 C cmul) (co D B2 cmul) caddc) (co (co A2 D cmul) (co C B2 cmul) caddc) caddc)) $;

--| Product of two differences. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mulsubd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C D cmin) cmul) (co (co (co A2 C cmul) (co D B2 cmul) caddc) (co (co A2 D cmul) (co C B2 cmul) caddc) cmin)) $;

--| Multiplication followed by the subtraction of a factor. (Contributed by Alexander van der Vekens, 28-Aug-2018.)
theorem mulsubfacd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) B2 cmin) (co (co A2 c1 cmin) B2 cmul)) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 12-Nov-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltadd2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co C A2 caddc) (co C B2 caddc) clt)) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jan-1997.)
theorem ltadd2i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co C A2 caddc) (co C B2 caddc) clt) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltadd2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co C A2 caddc) (co C B2 caddc) clt)) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem ltadd2dd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co C A2 caddc) (co C B2 caddc) clt) $;

--| Transitive law deduction for 'less than', 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 9-Jan-2006.)
theorem ltletrd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 C clt) $;

--| If a number is less than another number, and the other number is less than or equal to a third number, the first number is less than the third number. (Contributed by Alexander van der Vekens, 24-Mar-2018.)
theorem lelttrdi (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wi (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr A2 C clt)) $;

--| Positive implies nonzero. (Contributed by NM, 3-Oct-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem gt0ne0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wne A2 cc0) $;

--| A number which is less than zero is not zero. (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 13-Sep-2014.)
theorem lt0ne0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr A2 cc0 clt)) (wne A2 cc0) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than'. Part of definition 11.2.7(vi) of [HoTT], p. (varies). (Contributed by NM, 12-Nov-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltadd1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) clt)) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than or equal to'. Part of definition 11.2.7(vi) of [HoTT], p. (varies). (Contributed by NM, 18-Oct-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem leadd1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) cle)) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 26-Oct-1999.)
theorem leadd2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co C A2 caddc) (co C B2 caddc) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jan-1997.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltsubadd (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C clt) (wbr A2 (co C B2 caddc) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jan-1997.)
theorem ltsubadd2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C clt) (wbr A2 (co B2 C caddc) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 17-Nov-2004.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lesubadd (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C cle) (wbr A2 (co C B2 caddc) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 10-Aug-1999.)
theorem lesubadd2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C cle) (wbr A2 (co B2 C caddc) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between addition and subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 17-Nov-2004.)
theorem ltaddsub (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) C clt) (wbr A2 (co C B2 cmin) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between addition and subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 17-Nov-2004.)
theorem ltaddsub2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) C clt) (wbr B2 (co C A2 cmin) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between addition and subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 6-Apr-2005.)
theorem leaddsub (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) C cle) (wbr A2 (co C B2 cmin) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between and addition and subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 6-Apr-2005.)
theorem leaddsub2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) C cle) (wbr B2 (co C A2 cmin) cle)) $;

--| Swap subtrahends in an inequality. (Contributed by NM, 29-Sep-2005.)
theorem suble (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C cle) (wbr (co A2 C cmin) B2 cle)) $;

--| Swap subtrahends in an inequality. (Contributed by NM, 29-Sep-2005.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem lesub (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 (co B2 C cmin) cle) (wbr C (co B2 A2 cmin) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 4-Oct-1999.)
theorem ltsub23 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C clt) (wbr (co A2 C cmin) B2 clt)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 17-Nov-2004.)
theorem ltsub13 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 (co B2 C cmin) clt) (wbr C (co B2 A2 cmin) clt)) $;

--| Adding both sides of two 'less than or equal to' relations. (Contributed by NM, 17-Apr-2005.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem le2add (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr))) (wi (wa (wbr A2 C cle) (wbr B2 D cle)) (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) cle)) $;

--| Adding both sides of two 'less than' relations. Theorem I.25 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 15-Aug-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lt2add (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr))) (wi (wa (wbr A2 C clt) (wbr B2 D clt)) (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) clt)) $;

--| Adding both sides of two orderings. (Contributed by NM, 23-Dec-2007.)
theorem ltleadd (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr))) (wi (wa (wbr A2 C clt) (wbr B2 D cle)) (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) clt)) $;

--| Adding both sides of two orderings. (Contributed by NM, 15-Aug-2008.)
theorem leltadd (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr))) (wi (wa (wbr A2 C cle) (wbr B2 D clt)) (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) clt)) $;

--| The sum of 2 positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 1-Jun-2005.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem addgt0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) clt) $;

--| The sum of nonnegative and positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 28-Dec-2005.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem addgegt0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) clt) $;

--| The sum of nonnegative and positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 28-Dec-2005.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem addgtge0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 B2 cle))) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) clt) $;

--| The sum of 2 nonnegative numbers is nonnegative. (Contributed by NM, 17-Mar-2005.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem addge0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 cle))) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) cle) $;

--| Adding a positive number to another number increases it. (Contributed by NM, 17-Nov-2004.)
theorem ltaddpos (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr B2 (co B2 A2 caddc) clt)) $;

--| Adding a positive number to another number increases it. (Contributed by NM, 8-Apr-2005.)
theorem ltaddpos2 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr B2 (co A2 B2 caddc) clt)) $;

--| Subtracting a positive number from another number decreases it. (Contributed by NM, 17-Nov-2004.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem ltsubpos (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr (co B2 A2 cmin) B2 clt)) $;

--| Comparison of two numbers whose difference is positive. (Contributed by NM, 17-Nov-2004.)
theorem posdif (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr cc0 (co B2 A2 cmin) clt)) $;

--| Subtraction from both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 13-May-2004.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lesub1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin) cle)) $;

--| Subtraction of both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 29-Sep-2005.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lesub2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co C B2 cmin) (co C A2 cmin) cle)) $;

--| Subtraction from both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by FL, 3-Jan-2008.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltsub1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin) clt)) $;

--| Subtraction of both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 29-Sep-2005.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltsub2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co C B2 cmin) (co C A2 cmin) clt)) $;

--| Subtracting both sides of two 'less than' relations. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 14-Apr-2016.)
theorem lt2sub (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr))) (wi (wa (wbr A2 C clt) (wbr D B2 clt)) (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C D cmin) clt)) $;

--| Subtracting both sides of two 'less than or equal to' relations. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 14-Apr-2016.)
theorem le2sub (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr))) (wi (wa (wbr A2 C cle) (wbr D B2 cle)) (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) (co C D cmin) cle)) $;

--| Negative of both sides of 'less than'. Theorem I.23 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 27-Aug-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltneg (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (cneg B2) (cneg A2) clt)) $;

--| Contraposition of negative in 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 8-Nov-2004.)
theorem ltnegcon1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr (cneg A2) B2 clt) (wbr (cneg B2) A2 clt)) $;

--| Contraposition of negative in 'less than'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 25-Feb-2015.)
theorem ltnegcon2 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 (cneg B2) clt) (wbr B2 (cneg A2) clt)) $;

--| Negative of both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 12-Sep-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem leneg (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (cneg B2) (cneg A2) cle)) $;

--| Contraposition of negative in 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 10-May-2004.)
theorem lenegcon1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr (cneg A2) B2 cle) (wbr (cneg B2) A2 cle)) $;

--| Contraposition of negative in 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 8-Oct-2005.)
theorem lenegcon2 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 (cneg B2) cle) (wbr B2 (cneg A2) cle)) $;

--| Comparison of a number and its negative to zero. Theorem I.23 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1999.)
theorem lt0neg1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wb (wbr A2 cc0 clt) (wbr cc0 (cneg A2) clt)) $;

--| Comparison of a number and its negative to zero. (Contributed by NM, 10-May-2004.)
theorem lt0neg2 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wb (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr (cneg A2) cc0 clt)) $;

--| Comparison of a number and its negative to zero. (Contributed by NM, 10-May-2004.)
theorem le0neg1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wb (wbr A2 cc0 cle) (wbr cc0 (cneg A2) cle)) $;

--| Comparison of a number and its negative to zero. (Contributed by NM, 24-Aug-1999.)
theorem le0neg2 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wb (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr (cneg A2) cc0 cle)) $;

--| A number is less than or equal to itself plus a nonnegative number. (Contributed by NM, 21-Feb-2005.)
theorem addge01 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr cc0 B2 cle) (wbr A2 (co A2 B2 caddc) cle)) $;

--| A number is less than or equal to itself plus a nonnegative number. (Contributed by NM, 27-Jul-2005.)
theorem addge02 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr cc0 B2 cle) (wbr A2 (co B2 A2 caddc) cle)) $;

--| Two nonnegative numbers are zero iff their sum is zero. (Contributed by Jeff Madsen, 2-Sep-2009.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem add20 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 cle))) (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 caddc) cc0) (wa (wceq A2 cc0) (wceq B2 cc0))) $;

--| Nonnegative subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 14-Mar-2005.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subge0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmin) cle) (wbr B2 A2 cle)) $;

--| Nonpositive subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 20-Mar-2008.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem suble0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) cc0 cle) (wbr A2 B2 cle)) $;

--| The sum of a real number and a second real number is less then the real number iff the second real number is negative. (Contributed by Alexander van der Vekens, 30-May-2018.)
theorem leaddle0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) A2 cle) (wbr B2 cc0 cle)) $;

--| Nonnegative subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 27-Jul-2005.)
theorem subge02 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr cc0 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) A2 cle)) $;

--| Lemma to show a nonnegative number is zero. (Contributed by NM, 8-Oct-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lesub0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr B2 (co B2 A2 cmin) cle)) (wceq A2 cc0)) $;

--| The product of two negative numbers is positive. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 8-Jun-2009.)
theorem mullt0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr A2 cc0 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr B2 cc0 clt))) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) clt) $;

--| 0 is less than or equal to 1. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 29-Apr-2015.)
theorem _0le1:
  $ wbr cc0 c1 cle $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' is reflexive. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1999.)
theorem leidi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wbr A2 A2 cle $;

--| Positive means nonzero (useful for ordering theorems involving division). (Contributed by NM, 16-Sep-1999.)
theorem gt0ne0i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wne A2 cc0) $;

--| Positive implies nonzero. (Contributed by NM, 15-May-1999.)
theorem gt0ne0ii (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 A2 clt $ >
  $ wne A2 cc0 $;

--| Addition of 2 positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 16-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem addgt0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) clt) $;

--| Addition of 2 nonnegative numbers is nonnegative. (Contributed by NM, 28-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem addge0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 cle)) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) cle) $;

--| Addition of nonnegative and positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 25-Sep-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem addgegt0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) clt) $;

--| Addition of 2 positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 18-May-1999.)
theorem addgt0ii (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 A2 clt $ >
  $ wbr cc0 B2 clt $ >
  $ wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) clt $;

--| Two nonnegative numbers are zero iff their sum is zero. (Contributed by NM, 28-Jul-1999.)
theorem add20i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 cle)) (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 caddc) cc0) (wa (wceq A2 cc0) (wceq B2 cc0))) $;

--| Negative of both sides of 'less than'. Theorem I.23 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jan-1997.)
theorem ltnegi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (cneg B2) (cneg A2) clt) $;

--| Negative of both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1999.)
theorem lenegi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (cneg B2) (cneg A2) cle) $;

--| Contraposition of negative in 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1999.)
theorem ltnegcon2i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 (cneg B2) clt) (wbr B2 (cneg A2) clt) $;

--| Lemma to show a nonnegative number is zero. (Contributed by NM, 8-Oct-1999.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem lesub0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wb (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr B2 (co B2 A2 cmin) cle)) (wceq A2 cc0) $;

--| Adding a positive number to another number increases it. (Contributed by NM, 25-Aug-1999.)
theorem ltaddposi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr B2 (co B2 A2 caddc) clt) $;

--| Comparison of two numbers whose difference is positive. (Contributed by NM, 19-Aug-2001.)
theorem posdifi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr cc0 (co B2 A2 cmin) clt) $;

--| Contraposition of negative in 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1999.)
theorem ltnegcon1i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr (cneg A2) B2 clt) (wbr (cneg B2) A2 clt) $;

--| Contraposition of negative in 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 6-Apr-2005.)
theorem lenegcon1i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr (cneg A2) B2 cle) (wbr (cneg B2) A2 cle) $;

--| Nonnegative subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 13-Aug-2000.)
theorem subge0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmin) cle) (wbr B2 A2 cle) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than'. Theorem I.18 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jan-1997.)
theorem ltadd1i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) clt) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 11-Aug-1999.)
theorem leadd1i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) cle) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 11-Aug-1999.)
theorem leadd2i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co C A2 caddc) (co C B2 caddc) cle) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jan-1997.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem ltsubaddi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C clt) (wbr A2 (co C B2 caddc) clt) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 30-Sep-1999.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem lesubaddi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C cle) (wbr A2 (co C B2 caddc) cle) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 21-Jan-1997.)
theorem ltsubadd2i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C clt) (wbr A2 (co B2 C caddc) clt) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 3-Aug-1999.)
theorem lesubadd2i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C cle) (wbr A2 (co B2 C caddc) cle) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1999.)
theorem ltaddsubi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wb (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) C clt) (wbr A2 (co C B2 cmin) clt) $;

--| Adding both side of two inequalities. Theorem I.25 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1999.)
theorem lt2addi (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wcel D cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr A2 C clt) (wbr B2 D clt)) (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) clt) $;

--| Adding both side of two inequalities. (Contributed by NM, 16-Sep-1999.)
theorem le2addi (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wcel D cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr A2 C cle) (wbr B2 D cle)) (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) cle) $;

--| Positive implies nonzero. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem gt0ne0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne A2 cc0) $;

--| Something less than zero is not zero. Deduction form. (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem lt0ne0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne A2 cc0) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' is reflexive. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem leidd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 A2 cle) $;

