--| A number is less than or equal to itself plus a nonnegative number. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem addge02d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr cc0 B2 cle) (wbr A2 (co B2 A2 caddc) cle)) $;

--| Nonnegative subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subge0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmin) cle) (wbr B2 A2 cle)) $;

--| Nonpositive subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem suble0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) cc0 cle) (wbr A2 B2 cle)) $;

--| Nonnegative subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subge02d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr cc0 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) A2 cle)) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than'. Theorem I.18 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltadd1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) clt)) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem leadd1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) cle)) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem leadd2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co C A2 caddc) (co C B2 caddc) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltsubaddd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C clt) (wbr A2 (co C B2 caddc) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lesubaddd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C cle) (wbr A2 (co C B2 caddc) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltsubadd2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C clt) (wbr A2 (co B2 C caddc) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lesubadd2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C cle) (wbr A2 (co B2 C caddc) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltaddsubd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) C clt) (wbr A2 (co C B2 cmin) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 29-Dec-2016.)
theorem ltaddsub2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) C clt) (wbr B2 (co C A2 cmin) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between and addition and subtraction. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem leaddsub2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) C cle) (wbr B2 (co C A2 cmin) cle)) $;

--| Swap subtrahends in an inequality. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem subled (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C cmin) B2 cle) $;

--| Swap subtrahends in an inequality. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lesubd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 (co B2 C cmin) cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C (co B2 A2 cmin) cle) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltsub23d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) C clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C cmin) B2 clt) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between subtraction and addition. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltsub13d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 (co B2 C cmin) clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C (co B2 A2 cmin) clt) $;

--| Subtraction from both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lesub1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin) cle)) $;

--| Subtraction of both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lesub2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co C B2 cmin) (co C A2 cmin) cle)) $;

--| Subtraction from both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltsub1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin) clt)) $;

--| Subtraction of both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltsub2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co C B2 cmin) (co C A2 cmin) clt)) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than'. Theorem I.18 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem ltadd1dd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) clt) $;

--| Subtraction from both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem ltsub1dd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin) clt) $;

--| Subtraction of both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem ltsub2dd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co C B2 cmin) (co C A2 cmin) clt) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem leadd1dd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) cle) $;

--| Addition to both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem leadd2dd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co C A2 caddc) (co C B2 caddc) cle) $;

--| Subtraction from both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem lesub1dd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C cmin) (co B2 C cmin) cle) $;

--| Subtraction of both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 30-May-2016.)
theorem lesub2dd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co C B2 cmin) (co C A2 cmin) cle) $;

--| Adding both side of two inequalities. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem le2addd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 D cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) cle) $;

--| Subtracting both sides of two 'less than or equal to' relations. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem le2subd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 D cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 D cmin) (co C B2 cmin) cle) $;

--| Adding both sides of two orderings. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltleaddd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 C clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 D cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) clt) $;

--| Adding both sides of two orderings. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem leltaddd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 D clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) clt) $;

--| Adding both side of two inequalities. Theorem I.25 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lt2addd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 C clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 D clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) clt) $;

--| Subtracting both sides of two 'less than' relations. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lt2subd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 C clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 D clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 D cmin) (co C B2 cmin) clt) $;

--| Condition for a positive sum. (Contributed by Scott Fenton, 16-Dec-2017.)
theorem possumd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) clt) (wbr (cneg B2) A2 clt)) $;

--| When a subtraction gives a negative result. (Contributed by Glauco Siliprandi, 11-Dec-2019.)
theorem sublt0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) cc0 clt) (wbr A2 B2 clt)) $;

--| Addition and subtraction on one side of 'less than'. (Contributed by AV, 24-Nov-2018.)
theorem ltaddsublt (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr B2 C clt) (wbr (co (co A2 B2 caddc) C cmin) A2 clt)) $;

--| ` 1 <_ 1 ` . Common special case. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 16-Jul-2016.)
theorem _1le1:
  $ wbr c1 c1 cle $;

--| A positive sum must have a positive addend. Part of Definition 11.2.7(vi) of [HoTT], p. (varies). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Jan-2020.)
theorem gt0add (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 caddc) clt)) (wo (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) $;

--| Class of real apartness relation.
term creap: class;

--| Define real apartness. Definition in Section 11.2.1 of [HoTT], p. (varies). Although ` #RR ` is an apartness relation on the reals (see ~ df-ap for more discussion of apartness relations), for our purposes it is just a stepping stone to defining ` # ` which is an apartness relation on complex numbers. On the reals, ` #RR ` and ` # ` agree ( ~ apreap ). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Jan-2020.)
axiom df_reap {x3 y1: setvar}:
  $ wceq creap (copab x3 y1 (wa (wa (wcel (cv x3) cr) (wcel (cv y1) cr)) (wo (wbr (cv x3) (cv y1) clt) (wbr (cv y1) (cv x3) clt)))) $;

--| Real apartness in terms of classes. Beyond the development of ` # ` itself, proofs should use ~ reaplt instead. (New usage is discouraged.) (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Jan-2020.)
theorem reapval (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 creap) (wo (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr B2 A2 clt))) $;

--| Real apartness is irreflexive. Part of Definition 11.2.7(v) of [HoTT], p. (varies). Beyond the development of ` # ` itself, proofs should use ~ apirr instead. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Jan-2020.)
theorem reapirr (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wn (wbr A2 A2 creap)) $;

--| Existence of reciprocal of real number. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Jan-2020.)
theorem recexre {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr A2 cc0 creap)) (wrex x3 (wceq (co A2 (cv x3) cmul) c1) cr) $;

--| Real apartness is tight. Beyond the development of apartness itself, proofs should use ~ apti . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 30-Jan-2020.) (New usage is discouraged.)
theorem reapti (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wceq A2 B2) (wn (wbr A2 B2 creap))) $;

--| Existence of reciprocal of positive real number. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 6-Feb-2020.)
theorem recexgt0 {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wrex x3 (wa (wbr cc0 (cv x3) clt) (wceq (co A2 (cv x3) cmul) c1)) cr) $;

--| Class of complex apartness relation.
term cap: class;

--| Define complex apartness. Definition 6.1 of [Geuvers], p. 17. Two numbers are considered apart if it is possible to separate them. One common usage is that we can divide by a number if it is apart from zero (see for example ~ recclap which says that a number apart from zero has a reciprocal). The defining characteristics of an apartness are irreflexivity ( ~ apirr ), symmetry ( ~ apsym ), and cotransitivity ( ~ apcotr ). Apartness implies negated equality, as seen at ~ apne , and the converse would also follow if we assumed excluded middle. In addition, apartness of complex numbers is tight, which means that two numbers which are not apart are equal ( ~ apti ). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Jan-2020.)
axiom df_ap {x3 y1 u t s1 r: setvar}:
  $ wceq cap (copab x3 y1 (wrex r (wrex s1 (wrex t (wrex u (wa (wa (wceq (cv x3) (co (cv r) (co ci (cv s1) cmul) caddc)) (wceq (cv y1) (co (cv t) (co ci (cv u) cmul) caddc))) (wo (wbr (cv r) (cv t) creap) (wbr (cv s1) (cv u) creap))) cr) cr) cr) cr)) $;

--| ` _i ` times itself is minus 1. (Contributed by NM, 6-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem ixi:
  $ wceq (co ci ci cmul) (cneg c1) $;

--| The imaginary unit ` _i ` is not a real number. (Contributed by NM, 6-May-1999.)
theorem inelr:
  $ wn (wcel ci cr) $;

--| A real number times the imaginary unit is real only if the number is 0. (Contributed by NM, 28-May-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem rimul (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel (co ci A2 cmul) cr)) (wceq A2 cc0) $;

--| Decomposition of a real number into real part (itself) and imaginary part (zero). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 30-Jan-2020.)
theorem rereim (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wceq A2 (co B2 (co ci C cmul) caddc)))) (wa (wceq B2 A2) (wceq C cc0)) $;

--| Complex apartness and real apartness agree on the real numbers. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 31-Jan-2020.)
theorem apreap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr A2 B2 creap)) $;

--| Real apartness in terms of less than. Part of Definition 11.2.7(vi) of [HoTT], p. (varies). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 1-Feb-2020.)
theorem reaplt (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wo (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr B2 A2 clt))) $;

--| Real apartness in terms of less than (exclusive-or version). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Mar-2020.)
theorem reapltxor (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wxo (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr B2 A2 clt))) $;

--| One is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem _1ap0:
  $ wbr c1 cc0 cap $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than' by a positive number. Theorem I.19 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 15-May-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltmul1a (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wbr A2 B2 clt)) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) clt) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than' by a positive number. Theorem I.19 of [Apostol] p. 20. Part of Definition 11.2.7(vi) of [HoTT], p. (varies). (Contributed by NM, 13-Feb-2005.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltmul1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) clt)) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than or equal to' by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 21-Feb-2005.)
theorem lemul1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cle)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ reapmul1 . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 8-Feb-2020.)
theorem reapmul1lem (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cap)) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of real apartness by a real number apart from zero. Special case of ~ apmul1 . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 8-Feb-2020.)
theorem reapmul1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cap)) $;

--| Real addition respects apartness. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 13-Feb-2020.)
theorem reapadd1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) cap)) $;

--| Real negation respects apartness. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 13-Feb-2020.)
theorem reapneg (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr (cneg A2) (cneg B2) cap)) $;

--| Real apartness is cotransitive. Part of Definition 11.2.7(v) of [HoTT], p. (varies). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 16-Feb-2020.)
theorem reapcotr (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wi (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wo (wbr A2 C cap) (wbr B2 C cap))) $;

--| Left extensionality for multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Feb-2020.)
theorem remulext1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wi (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cap) (wbr A2 B2 cap)) $;

--| Right extensionality for real multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem remulext2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wcel C cr)) (wi (wbr (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul) cap) (wbr A2 B2 cap)) $;

--| The square of a real number apart from zero is positive. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 7-Feb-2020.)
theorem apsqgt0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wbr cc0 (co A2 A2 cmul) clt) $;

--| The representation of complex numbers in terms of real and imaginary parts is unique. Proposition 10-1.3 of [Gleason] p. 130. (Contributed by NM, 9-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem cru (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr))) (wb (wceq (co A2 (co ci B2 cmul) caddc) (co C (co ci D cmul) caddc)) (wa (wceq A2 C) (wceq B2 D))) $;

--| Complex apartness in terms of real and imaginary parts. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 12-Feb-2020.)
theorem apreim (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr))) (wb (wbr (co A2 (co ci B2 cmul) caddc) (co C (co ci D cmul) caddc) cap) (wo (wbr A2 C cap) (wbr B2 D cap))) $;

--| Complex multiplication in terms of real and imaginary parts. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulreim (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr))) (wceq (co (co A2 (co ci B2 cmul) caddc) (co C (co ci D cmul) caddc) cmul) (co (co (co A2 C cmul) (cneg (co B2 D cmul)) caddc) (co ci (co (co C B2 cmul) (co D A2 cmul) caddc) cmul) caddc)) $;

--| Apartness is irreflexive. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 16-Feb-2020.)
theorem apirr (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wn (wbr A2 A2 cap)) $;

--| Apartness is symmetric. This theorem for real numbers is part of Definition 11.2.7(v) of [HoTT], p. (varies). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 16-Feb-2020.)
theorem apsym (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr B2 A2 cap)) $;

--| Apartness is cotransitive. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 16-Feb-2020.)
theorem apcotr (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wcel C cc)) (wi (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wo (wbr A2 C cap) (wbr B2 C cap))) $;

--| Addition respects apartness. Analogue of ~ addcan for apartness. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 13-Feb-2020.)
theorem apadd1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wcel C cc)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr (co A2 C caddc) (co B2 C caddc) cap)) $;

--| Addition respects apartness. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 16-Feb-2020.)
theorem apadd2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wcel C cc)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr (co C A2 caddc) (co C B2 caddc) cap)) $;

--| Strong extensionality for addition. Given excluded middle, apartness would be equivalent to negated equality and this would follow readily (for all operations) from ~ oveq12 . For us, it is proved a different way. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 15-Feb-2020.)
theorem addext (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wcel D cc))) (wi (wbr (co A2 B2 caddc) (co C D caddc) cap) (wo (wbr A2 C cap) (wbr B2 D cap))) $;

--| Negation respects apartness. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 14-Feb-2020.)
theorem apneg (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr (cneg A2) (cneg B2) cap)) $;

--| Left extensionality for complex multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulext1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wcel C cc)) (wi (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cap) (wbr A2 B2 cap)) $;

--| Right extensionality for complex multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulext2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wcel C cc)) (wi (wbr (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul) cap) (wbr A2 B2 cap)) $;

--| Strong extensionality for multiplication. Given excluded middle, apartness would be equivalent to negated equality and this would follow readily (for all operations) from ~ oveq12 . For us, it is proved a different way. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulext (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wcel D cc))) (wi (wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) (co C D cmul) cap) (wo (wbr A2 C cap) (wbr B2 D cap))) $;

--| A product apart from zero. Lemma 2.13 of [Geuvers], p. 6. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulap0r (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) cc0 cap)) (wa (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) $;

--| A square is nonnegative. Lemma 2.35 of [Geuvers], p. 9. (Contributed by NM, 23-May-2007.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem msqge0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 (co A2 A2 cmul) cle) $;

--| A square is nonnegative. (Contributed by NM, 14-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 19-Nov-2011.)
theorem msqge0i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 (co A2 A2 cmul) cle $;

--| A square is nonnegative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem msqge0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 (co A2 A2 cmul) cle) $;

--| The product of two nonnegative numbers is nonnegative. (Contributed by NM, 8-Oct-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mulge0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 cle))) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) cle) $;

--| The product of two nonnegative numbers is nonnegative. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-1999.)
theorem mulge0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 cle)) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) cle) $;

--| The product of two nonnegative numbers is nonnegative. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem mulge0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) cle) $;

--| Complex apartness is tight. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem apti (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wb (wceq A2 B2) (wn (wbr A2 B2 cap))) $;

--| Apartness implies negated equality. We cannot in general prove the converse, which is the whole point of having separate notations for apartness and negated equality. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem apne (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wi (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wne A2 B2)) $;

--| '<_' implies 'less than' is 'apart'. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 13-Aug-2021.)
theorem leltap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr A2 B2 cle)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr B2 A2 cap)) $;

--| Positive implies apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem gt0ap0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $;

--| Positive means apart from zero (useful for ordering theorems involving division). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem gt0ap0i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $;

--| Positive implies apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem gt0ap0ii (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 A2 clt $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $;

--| Positive implies apart from zero. Because of the way we define ` # ` , ` A ` must be an element of ` RR ` , not just ` RR* ` . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem gt0ap0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $;

--| A number is apart from zero iff its negative is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem negap0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wb (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr (cneg A2) cc0 cap)) $;

--| Less than in terms of non-strict order and apartness. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem ltleap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wa (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr A2 B2 cap))) $;

--| 'Less than' implies apart. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 12-Aug-2021.)
theorem ltap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr A2 B2 clt)) (wbr B2 A2 cap) $;

--| 'Greater than' implies apart. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 12-Aug-2021.)
theorem gtapii (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wbr A2 B2 clt $ >
  $ wbr B2 A2 cap $;

--| 'Less than' implies apart. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 12-Aug-2021.)
theorem ltapii (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wbr A2 B2 clt $ >
  $ wbr A2 B2 cap $;

--| 'Less than' implies apart. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 12-Aug-2021.)
theorem ltapi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr B2 A2 cap) $;

--| 'Greater than' implies apart. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 12-Aug-2021.)
theorem gtapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 A2 cap) $;

--| 'Less than' implies apart. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 12-Aug-2021.)
theorem ltapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cap) $;

--| '<_' implies 'less than' is 'apart'. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 13-Aug-2021.)
theorem leltapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr B2 A2 cap)) $;

--| A nonnegative number is apart from zero if and only if it is positive. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 11-Aug-2021.)
theorem ap0gt0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wb (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) $;

--| A nonzero nonnegative number is positive. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 11-Aug-2021.)
theorem ap0gt0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 clt) $;

--| Two numbers apart from each other have difference apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 12-Aug-2021.)
theorem subap0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 cmin) cc0 cap) $;

--| Lemma for ~ recexap . (Contributed by Eric Schmidt, 23-May-2007.)
theorem recextlem1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wceq (co (co A2 (co ci B2 cmul) caddc) (co A2 (co ci B2 cmul) cmin) cmul) (co (co A2 A2 cmul) (co B2 B2 cmul) caddc)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ recexap . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 20-Feb-2020.)
theorem recexaplem2 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr (co A2 (co ci B2 cmul) caddc) cc0 cap)) (wbr (co (co A2 A2 cmul) (co B2 B2 cmul) caddc) cc0 cap) $;

--| Existence of reciprocal of nonzero complex number. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 20-Feb-2020.)
theorem recexap {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wrex x3 (wceq (co A2 (cv x3) cmul) c1) cc) $;

--| The product of two numbers apart from zero is apart from zero. Lemma 2.15 of [Geuvers], p. 6. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulap0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap))) (wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) cc0 cap) $;

--| The product of two numbers apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulap0b (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wb (wa (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) cc0 cap)) $;

--| The product of two numbers apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulap0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) cc0 cap $;

--| The product of two numbers apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulap0bd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wa (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) cc0 cap)) $;

--| The product of two numbers apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 23-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulap0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) cc0 cap) $;

--| A factor of a complex number apart from zero is apart from zero. Partial converse of ~ mulap0d and consequence of ~ mulap0bd . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulap0bad (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $;

--| A factor of a complex number apart from zero is apart from zero. Partial converse of ~ mulap0d and consequence of ~ mulap0bd . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulap0bbd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $;

--| Cancellation law for multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulcanapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| Cancellation law for multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulcanap2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| Cancellation of a nonzero factor on the left in an equation. One-way deduction form of ~ mulcanapd . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulcanapad (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Cancellation of a nonzero factor on the right in an equation. One-way deduction form of ~ mulcanap2d . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulcanap2ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Cancellation law for multiplication (full theorem form). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulcanap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wb (wceq (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| Cancellation law for multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulcanap2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wb (wceq (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| Cancellation law for multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem mulcanapi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wbr C cc0 cap $ >
  $ wb (wceq (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul)) (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Property of numbers whose product equals their sum. Equation 5 of [Kreyszig] p. 12. (Contributed by NM, 13-Nov-2006.)
theorem muleqadd (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cmul) (co A2 B2 caddc)) (wceq (co (co A2 c1 cmin) (co B2 c1 cmin) cmul) c1)) $;

--| Existential uniqueness of reciprocals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem receuap {x3: setvar} (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wreu x3 (wceq (co B2 (cv x3) cmul) A2) cc) $;

--| Extend class notation to include division.
term cdiv: class;

--| Define division. Theorem ~ divmulap relates it to multiplication, and ~ divclap and ~ redivclap prove its closure laws. (Contributed by NM, 2-Feb-1995.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 1-Apr-2014.) (New usage is discouraged.)
axiom df_div {x3 y1 z: setvar}:
  $ wceq cdiv (cmpt2 x3 y1 cc (cdif cc (csn cc0)) (crio z (wceq (co (cv y1) (cv z) cmul) (cv x3)) cc)) $;

--| Value of division: the (unique) element ` x ` such that ` ( B x. x ) = A ` . This is meaningful only when ` B ` is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 21-Feb-2020.)
theorem divvalap {x3: setvar} (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) (crio x3 (wceq (co B2 (cv x3) cmul) A2) cc)) $;

--| Relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem divmulap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wb (wceq (co A2 C cdiv) B2) (wceq (co C B2 cmul) A2)) $;

--| Relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem divmulap2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wb (wceq (co A2 C cdiv) B2) (wceq A2 (co C B2 cmul))) $;

--| Relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem divmulap3 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wb (wceq (co A2 C cdiv) B2) (wceq A2 (co B2 C cmul))) $;

--| Closure law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem divclap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wcel (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc) $;

--| Closure law for reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem recclap (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wcel (co c1 A2 cdiv) cc) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap2 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co B2 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cmul) A2) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) B2 cmul) A2) $;

--| A ratio is zero iff the numerator is zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem diveqap0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0) (wceq A2 cc0)) $;

--| The ratio of numbers apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem divap0b (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wb (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0 cap)) $;

--| The ratio of numbers apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 22-Feb-2020.)
theorem divap0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap))) (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0 cap) $;

--| The reciprocal of a number apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem recap0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wbr (co c1 A2 cdiv) cc0 cap) $;

--| Multiplication of a number and its reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem recidap (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co A2 (co c1 A2 cdiv) cmul) c1) $;

--| Multiplication of a number and its reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem recidap2 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co (co c1 A2 cdiv) A2 cmul) c1) $;

--| Relationship between division and reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 24-Feb-2020.)
theorem divrecap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co A2 (co c1 B2 cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| Relationship between division and reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem divrecap2 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co (co c1 B2 cdiv) A2 cmul)) $;

--| An associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem divassap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) C cdiv) (co A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| A commutative/associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem div23ap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) B2 cmul)) $;

--| A commutative/associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem div32ap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wcel C cc)) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) C cmul) (co A2 (co C B2 cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| A commutative/associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem div13ap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wcel C cc)) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) C cmul) (co (co C B2 cdiv) A2 cmul)) $;

--| A commutative/associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem div12ap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cmul) (co B2 (co A2 C cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| Distribution of division over addition. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem divdirap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) caddc)) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap3 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co (co B2 A2 cmul) B2 cdiv) A2) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap4 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) B2 cdiv) A2) $;

--| One-to-one relationship for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem div11ap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wb (wceq (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| A number divided by itself is one. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem dividap (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co A2 A2 cdiv) c1) $;

--| Division into zero is zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem div0ap (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co cc0 A2 cdiv) cc0) $;

--| A number divided by 1 is itself. (Contributed by NM, 9-Jan-2002.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem div1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wceq (co A2 c1 cdiv) A2) $;

--| 1 divided by 1 is 1 (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 7-Dec-2018.)
theorem _1div1e1:
  $ wceq (co c1 c1 cdiv) c1 $;

--| Equality in terms of unit ratio. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem diveqap1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) c1) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| Move negative sign inside of a division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem divnegap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (cneg (co A2 B2 cdiv)) (co (cneg A2) B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Distribution of division over subtraction. (Contributed by NM, 4-Mar-2005.)
theorem divsubdirap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) cmin)) $;

--| A number is equal to the reciprocal of its reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem recrecap (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co c1 (co c1 A2 cdiv) cdiv) A2) $;

--| Reciprocal is one-to-one. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem rec11ap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap))) (wb (wceq (co c1 A2 cdiv) (co c1 B2 cdiv)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| Mutual reciprocals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem rec11rap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap))) (wb (wceq (co c1 A2 cdiv) B2) (wceq (co c1 B2 cdiv) A2)) $;

--| Multiplication of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem divmuldivap (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel D cc) (wbr D cc0 cap)))) (wceq (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 D cdiv) cmul) (co (co A2 B2 cmul) (co C D cmul) cdiv)) $;

--| Division of two ratios. Theorem I.15 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem divdivdivap (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap))) (wa (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel D cc) (wbr D cc0 cap)))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co C D cdiv) cdiv) (co (co A2 D cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cdiv)) $;

--| Cancellation of common factor in a ratio. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap5 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul) cdiv) (co A2 B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Swap the denominators in the product of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divmul13ap (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel D cc) (wbr D cc0 cap)))) (wceq (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 D cdiv) cmul) (co (co B2 C cdiv) (co A2 D cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| Swap the numerators in the product of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divmul24ap (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel D cc) (wbr D cc0 cap)))) (wceq (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 D cdiv) cmul) (co (co A2 D cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| Cross-multiply in an equality of ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divmuleqap (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel D cc) (wbr D cc0 cap)))) (wb (wceq (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 D cdiv)) (wceq (co A2 D cmul) (co B2 C cmul))) $;

--| The reciprocal of a ratio. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem recdivap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap))) (wceq (co c1 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cdiv) (co B2 A2 cdiv)) $;

--| Cancellation of inverted fractions. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap6 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co B2 A2 cdiv) cmul) c1) $;

--| Swap denominators in a division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divdiv32ap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Cancel equal divisors in a division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap7 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) cdiv) (co A2 B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Cancellation law for division and multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem dmdcanap (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wcel C cc)) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co C A2 cdiv) cmul) (co C B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Division into a fraction. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divdivap1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) C cdiv) (co A2 (co B2 C cmul) cdiv)) $;

--| Division by a fraction. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divdivap2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cdiv) (co (co A2 C cmul) B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Division into a reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem recdivap2 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap))) (wceq (co (co c1 A2 cdiv) B2 cdiv) (co c1 (co A2 B2 cmul) cdiv)) $;

--| Cancellation in a double division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem ddcanap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap))) (wceq (co A2 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cdiv) B2) $;

--| Addition of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divadddivap (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel D cc) (wbr D cc0 cap)))) (wceq (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 D cdiv) caddc) (co (co (co A2 D cmul) (co B2 C cmul) caddc) (co C D cmul) cdiv)) $;

--| Subtraction of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem divsubdivap (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc)) (wa (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel D cc) (wbr D cc0 cap)))) (wceq (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 D cdiv) cmin) (co (co (co A2 D cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cmin) (co C D cmul) cdiv)) $;

--| Two numbers whose reciprocals sum to 1 are called "conjugates" and satisfy this relationship. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem conjmulap (P Q: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel P cc) (wbr P cc0 cap)) (wa (wcel Q cc) (wbr Q cc0 cap))) (wb (wceq (co (co c1 P cdiv) (co c1 Q cdiv) caddc) c1) (wceq (co (co P c1 cmin) (co Q c1 cmin) cmul) c1)) $;

--| Closure law for reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem rerecclap (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr A2 cc0 cap)) (wcel (co c1 A2 cdiv) cr) $;

--| Closure law for division of reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem redivclap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wcel (co A2 B2 cdiv) cr) $;

--| A number equal to its negative is zero. (Contributed by NM, 12-Jul-2005.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem eqneg (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wb (wceq A2 (cneg A2)) (wceq A2 cc0)) $;

--| A complex number equals its negative iff it is zero. Deduction form of ~ eqneg . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem eqnegd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq A2 (cneg A2)) (wceq A2 cc0)) $;

--| If a complex number equals its own negative, it is zero. One-way deduction form of ~ eqneg . (Contributed by David Moews, 28-Feb-2017.)
theorem eqnegad (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 (cneg A2)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 cc0) $;

--| Quotient of two negatives. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem div2negap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (co (cneg A2) (cneg B2) cdiv) (co A2 B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Move negative sign inside of a division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem divneg2ap (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wceq (cneg (co A2 B2 cdiv)) (co A2 (cneg B2) cdiv)) $;

--| Closure law for reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem recclapzi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wcel (co c1 A2 cdiv) cc) $;

--| The reciprocal of a number apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem recap0apzi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr (co c1 A2 cdiv) cc0 cap) $;

--| Multiplication of a number and its reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem recidapzi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wceq (co A2 (co c1 A2 cdiv) cmul) c1) $;

--| A number divided by 1 is itself. (Contributed by NM, 9-Jan-2002.)
theorem div1i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wceq (co A2 c1 cdiv) A2 $;

--| A number equal to its negative is zero. (Contributed by NM, 29-May-1999.)
theorem eqnegi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wb (wceq A2 (cneg A2)) (wceq A2 cc0) $;

--| Closure law for reciprocal. (Contributed by NM, 30-Apr-2005.)
theorem recclapi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wcel (co c1 A2 cdiv) cc $;

--| Multiplication of a number and its reciprocal. (Contributed by NM, 9-Feb-1995.)
theorem recidapi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co A2 (co c1 A2 cdiv) cmul) c1 $;

--| A number is equal to the reciprocal of its reciprocal. Theorem I.10 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by NM, 9-Feb-1995.)
theorem recrecapi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co c1 (co c1 A2 cdiv) cdiv) A2 $;

--| A number divided by itself is one. (Contributed by NM, 9-Feb-1995.)
theorem dividapi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co A2 A2 cdiv) c1 $;

--| Division into zero is zero. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1999.)
theorem div0api (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co cc0 A2 cdiv) cc0 $;

--| Closure law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem divclapzi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr B2 cc0 cap) (wcel (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap1zi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr B2 cc0 cap) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) B2 cmul) A2) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap2zi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr B2 cc0 cap) (wceq (co B2 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cmul) A2) $;

--| Relationship between division and reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem divrecapzi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr B2 cc0 cap) (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co A2 (co c1 B2 cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap3zi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr B2 cc0 cap) (wceq (co (co B2 A2 cmul) B2 cdiv) A2) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 27-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap4zi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr B2 cc0 cap) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) B2 cdiv) A2) $;

--| Reciprocal is one-to-one. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem rec11api (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wb (wceq (co c1 A2 cdiv) (co c1 B2 cdiv)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| Closure law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divclapi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wcel (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap2i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co B2 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cmul) A2 $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap1i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) B2 cmul) A2 $;

--| Relationship between division and reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divrecapi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co A2 (co c1 B2 cdiv) cmul) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap3i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co B2 A2 cmul) B2 cdiv) A2 $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap4i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) B2 cdiv) A2 $;

--| The ratio of numbers apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divap0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0 cap $;

--| Reciprocal is one-to-one. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem rec11apii (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wb (wceq (co c1 A2 cdiv) (co c1 B2 cdiv)) (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| An associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divassapzi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr C cc0 cap) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) C cdiv) (co A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| Relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divmulapzi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr B2 cc0 cap) (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) C) (wceq (co B2 C cmul) A2)) $;

--| Distribution of division over addition. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divdirapzi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wi (wbr C cc0 cap) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) caddc)) $;

--| Swap denominators in a division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 28-Feb-2020.)
theorem divdiv23apzi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr B2 cc0 cap) (wbr C cc0 cap)) (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem divmulapi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) C) (wceq (co B2 C cmul) A2) $;

--| Swap denominators in a division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem divdiv32api (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr C cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) B2 cdiv) $;

--| An associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem divassapi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wbr C cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) C cdiv) (co A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cmul) $;

--| Distribution of division over addition. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem divdirapi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wbr C cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) caddc) $;

--| A commutative/associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem div23api (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wbr C cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) B2 cmul) $;

--| One-to-one relationship for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem div11api (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wbr C cc0 cap $ >
  $ wb (wceq (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv)) (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Multiplication of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem divmuldivapi (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wcel D cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr D cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co C D cdiv) cmul) (co (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 D cmul) cdiv) $;

--| Swap denominators of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem divmul13api (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wcel D cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr D cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co C D cdiv) cmul) (co (co C B2 cdiv) (co A2 D cdiv) cmul) $;

--| Addition of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem divadddivapi (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wcel D cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr D cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co C D cdiv) caddc) (co (co (co A2 D cmul) (co C B2 cmul) caddc) (co B2 D cmul) cdiv) $;

--| Division of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem divdivdivapi (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wcel B2 cc $ >
  $ wcel C cc $ >
  $ wcel D cc $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr D cc0 cap $ >
  $ wbr C cc0 cap $ >
  $ wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co C D cdiv) cdiv) (co (co A2 D cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cdiv) $;

--| Closure law for reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem rerecclapzi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wcel (co c1 A2 cdiv) cr) $;

--| Closure law for reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem rerecclapi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wbr A2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wcel (co c1 A2 cdiv) cr $;

--| Closure law for division of reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem redivclapzi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr B2 cc0 cap) (wcel (co A2 B2 cdiv) cr) $;

--| Closure law for division of reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem redivclapi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wbr B2 cc0 cap $ >
  $ wcel (co A2 B2 cdiv) cr $;

--| A number divided by 1 is itself. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem div1d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 c1 cdiv) A2) $;

--| Closure law for reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem recclapd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co c1 A2 cdiv) cc) $;

--| The reciprocal of a number apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem recap0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co c1 A2 cdiv) cc0 cap) $;

--| Multiplication of a number and its reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem recidapd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co c1 A2 cdiv) cmul) c1) $;

--| Multiplication of a number and its reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem recidap2d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co c1 A2 cdiv) A2 cmul) c1) $;

--| A number is equal to the reciprocal of its reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem recrecapd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co c1 (co c1 A2 cdiv) cdiv) A2) $;

--| A number divided by itself is one. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem dividapd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 A2 cdiv) c1) $;

--| Division into zero is zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem div0apd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co cc0 A2 cdiv) cc0) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of complex apartness by a complex number apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 20-Mar-2020.)
theorem apmul1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cc) (wcel B2 cc) (wa (wcel C cc) (wbr C cc0 cap))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cap) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cap)) $;

--| Closure law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem divclapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) B2 cmul) A2) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co B2 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cmul) A2) $;

--| Relationship between division and reciprocal. Theorem I.9 of [Apostol] p. 18. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem divrecapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co A2 (co c1 B2 cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| Relationship between division and reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem divrecap2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co (co c1 B2 cdiv) A2 cmul)) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap3d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co B2 A2 cmul) B2 cdiv) A2) $;

--| A cancellation law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem divcanap4d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) B2 cdiv) A2) $;

--| If a ratio is zero, the numerator is zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Mar-2020.)
theorem diveqap0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 cc0) $;

--| Equality in terms of unit ratio. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Mar-2020.)
theorem diveqap1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) c1) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| The quotient of two complex numbers is one iff they are equal. Deduction form of ~ diveqap1 . Generalization of ~ diveqap1d . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Mar-2020.)
theorem diveqap1ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) c1) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| A fraction of complex numbers is zero iff its numerator is. Deduction form of ~ diveqap0 . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Mar-2020.)
theorem diveqap0ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0) (wceq A2 cc0)) $;

--| If two complex numbers are apart, their quotient is apart from one. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 20-Mar-2020.)
theorem divap1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) c1 cap) $;

--| A ratio is zero iff the numerator is zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Mar-2020.)
theorem divap0bd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0 cap)) $;

--| Move negative sign inside of a division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Mar-2020.)
theorem divnegapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cneg (co A2 B2 cdiv)) (co (cneg A2) B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Move negative sign inside of a division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Mar-2020.)
theorem divneg2apd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (cneg (co A2 B2 cdiv)) (co A2 (cneg B2) cdiv)) $;

--| Quotient of two negatives. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 19-Mar-2020.)
theorem div2negapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (cneg A2) (cneg B2) cdiv) (co A2 B2 cdiv)) $;

--| The ratio of numbers apart from zero is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem divap0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) cc0 cap) $;

--| The reciprocal of a ratio. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem recdivapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co c1 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cdiv) (co B2 A2 cdiv)) $;

--| Division into a reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem recdivap2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co c1 A2 cdiv) B2 cdiv) (co c1 (co A2 B2 cmul) cdiv)) $;

--| Cancellation of inverted fractions. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem divcanap6d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co B2 A2 cdiv) cmul) c1) $;

--| Cancellation in a double division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem ddcanapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cdiv) B2) $;

--| Reciprocal is one-to-one. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 3-Mar-2020.)
theorem rec11apd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co c1 A2 cdiv) (co c1 B2 cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 8-Mar-2020.)
theorem divmulapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 B2 cdiv) C) (wceq (co B2 C cmul) A2)) $;

--| A commutative/associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 8-Mar-2020.)
theorem div32apd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
