  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cdiv) (co (co A2 C cmul) B2 cdiv)) $;

--| Relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Mar-2020.)
theorem divmulap2d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 C cdiv) B2) (wceq A2 (co C B2 cmul))) $;

--| Relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Mar-2020.)
theorem divmulap3d (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wb (wceq (co A2 C cdiv) B2) (wceq A2 (co B2 C cmul))) $;

--| An associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Mar-2020.)
theorem divassapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) C cdiv) (co A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| A commutative/associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Mar-2020.)
theorem div12apd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cmul) (co B2 (co A2 C cdiv) cmul)) $;

--| A commutative/associative law for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Mar-2020.)
theorem div23apd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmul) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) B2 cmul)) $;

--| Distribution of division over addition. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Mar-2020.)
theorem divdirapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 caddc) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) caddc)) $;

--| Distribution of division over subtraction. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Mar-2020.)
theorem divsubdirapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cmin) C cdiv) (co (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) cmin)) $;

--| One-to-one relationship for division. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 2-Mar-2020.)
theorem div11apd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv)) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq A2 B2) $;

--| Multiplication of two ratios. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 30-Jul-2021.)
theorem divmuldivapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr D cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co C D cdiv) cmul) (co (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 D cmul) cdiv)) $;

--| Closure law for reciprocal. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem rerecclapd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co c1 A2 cdiv) cr) $;

--| Closure law for division of reals. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem redivclapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr B2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 B2 cdiv) cr) $;

--| Move LHS left multiplication to RHS. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 10-Jun-2020.)
theorem mvllmulapd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cc) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq (co A2 B2 cmul) C) $ >
  $ wi ph (wceq B2 (co C A2 cdiv)) $;

--| A number is less than itself plus 1. (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-2001.)
theorem ltp1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wbr A2 (co A2 c1 caddc) clt) $;

--| A number is less than or equal to itself plus 1. (Contributed by NM, 5-Jan-2006.)
theorem lep1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wbr A2 (co A2 c1 caddc) cle) $;

--| A number minus 1 is less than itself. (Contributed by NM, 9-Apr-2006.)
theorem ltm1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wbr (co A2 c1 cmin) A2 clt) $;

--| A number minus 1 is less than or equal to itself. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 2-Oct-2015.)
theorem lem1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cr) (wbr (co A2 c1 cmin) A2 cle) $;

--| A transitive property of 'less than or equal' and plus 1. (Contributed by NM, 5-Aug-2005.)
theorem letrp1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr A2 B2 cle)) (wbr A2 (co B2 c1 caddc) cle) $;

--| A transitive property of plus 1 and 'less than or equal'. (Contributed by NM, 16-Aug-2005.)
theorem p1le (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr (co A2 c1 caddc) B2 cle)) (wbr A2 B2 cle) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive number is positive. Exercise 4 of [Apostol] p. 21. (Contributed by NM, 25-Aug-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem recgt0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wbr cc0 (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt) $;

--| Infer that a multiplicand is positive from a positive multiplier and positive product. See ~ prodgt0 for the same theorem with ` 0 < A ` replaced by the weaker condition ` 0 <_ A ` . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 29-Feb-2020.)
theorem prodgt0gt0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) clt))) (wbr cc0 B2 clt) $;

--| Infer that a multiplicand is positive from a nonnegative multiplier and positive product. (Contributed by NM, 24-Apr-2005.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem prodgt0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) clt))) (wbr cc0 B2 clt) $;

--| Infer that a multiplier is positive from a nonnegative multiplicand and positive product. (Contributed by NM, 24-Apr-2005.)
theorem prodgt02 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 B2 cle) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) clt))) (wbr cc0 A2 clt) $;

--| Infer that a multiplicand is nonnegative from a positive multiplier and nonnegative product. (Contributed by NM, 2-Jul-2005.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem prodge0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) cle))) (wbr cc0 B2 cle) $;

--| Infer that a multiplier is nonnegative from a positive multiplicand and nonnegative product. (Contributed by NM, 2-Jul-2005.)
theorem prodge02 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 B2 clt) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) cle))) (wbr cc0 A2 cle) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than' by a positive number. Theorem I.19 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 13-Feb-2005.)
theorem ltmul2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul) clt)) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than or equal to' by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 16-Mar-2005.)
theorem lemul2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul) cle)) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than or equal to' by a nonnegative number. Part of Definition 11.2.7(vi) of [HoTT], p. (varies). (Contributed by NM, 21-Feb-2005.)
theorem lemul1a (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C cle))) (wbr A2 B2 cle)) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cle) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than or equal to' by a nonnegative number. (Contributed by Paul Chapman, 7-Sep-2007.)
theorem lemul2a (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C cle))) (wbr A2 B2 cle)) (wbr (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul) cle) $;

--| Comparison of product of two positive numbers. (Contributed by NM, 30-Dec-2005.)
theorem ltmul12a (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr A2 B2 clt))) (wa (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 C cle) (wbr C D clt)))) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 D cmul) clt) $;

--| Comparison of product of two nonnegative numbers. (Contributed by NM, 22-Feb-2008.)
theorem lemul12b (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wa (wcel D cr) (wbr cc0 D cle)))) (wi (wa (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr C D cle)) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 D cmul) cle)) $;

--| Comparison of product of two nonnegative numbers. (Contributed by NM, 22-Feb-2008.)
theorem lemul12a (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C cle)) (wcel D cr))) (wi (wa (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr C D cle)) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 D cmul) cle)) $;

--| The product of two numbers greater than 1 is greater than 1. (Contributed by NM, 13-Feb-2005.)
theorem mulgt1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr c1 A2 clt) (wbr c1 B2 clt))) (wbr c1 (co A2 B2 cmul) clt) $;

--| Multiplication by a number greater than 1. (Contributed by NM, 24-Dec-2005.)
theorem ltmulgt11 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wb (wbr c1 B2 clt) (wbr A2 (co A2 B2 cmul) clt)) $;

--| Multiplication by a number greater than 1. (Contributed by NM, 24-Dec-2005.)
theorem ltmulgt12 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wb (wbr c1 B2 clt) (wbr A2 (co B2 A2 cmul) clt)) $;

--| Multiplication by a number greater than or equal to 1. (Contributed by NM, 17-Dec-2005.)
theorem lemulge11 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr c1 B2 cle))) (wbr A2 (co A2 B2 cmul) cle) $;

--| Multiplication by a number greater than or equal to 1. (Contributed by Paul Chapman, 21-Mar-2011.)
theorem lemulge12 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr c1 B2 cle))) (wbr A2 (co B2 A2 cmul) cle) $;

--| Division of both sides of 'less than' by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 10-Oct-2004.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltdiv1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) clt)) $;

--| Division of both sides of a less than or equal to relation by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 18-Nov-2004.)
theorem lediv1 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) cle)) $;

--| Division of a positive number by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 28-Sep-2005.)
theorem gt0div (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wb (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cdiv) clt)) $;

--| Division of a nonnegative number by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 28-Sep-2005.)
theorem ge0div (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wb (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cle)) $;

--| The ratio of two positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 12-Oct-1999.)
theorem divgt0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cdiv) clt) $;

--| The ratio of nonnegative and positive numbers is nonnegative. (Contributed by NM, 27-Sep-1999.)
theorem divge0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cle) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 12-Oct-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltmuldiv (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co A2 C cmul) B2 clt) (wbr A2 (co B2 C cdiv) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 18-Nov-2004.)
theorem ltmuldiv2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co C A2 cmul) B2 clt) (wbr A2 (co B2 C cdiv) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 18-Nov-2004.)
theorem ltdivmul (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) B2 clt) (wbr A2 (co C B2 cmul) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 9-Dec-2005.)
theorem ledivmul (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) B2 cle) (wbr A2 (co C B2 cmul) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem ltdivmul2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) B2 clt) (wbr A2 (co B2 C cmul) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 8-Jan-2006.)
theorem lt2mul2div (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wa (wcel C cr) (wa (wcel D cr) (wbr cc0 D clt)))) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cmul) (co C D cmul) clt) (wbr (co A2 D cdiv) (co C B2 cdiv) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal to' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 9-Dec-2005.)
theorem ledivmul2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) B2 cle) (wbr A2 (co B2 C cmul) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 10-Mar-2006.)
theorem lemuldiv (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co A2 C cmul) B2 cle) (wbr A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cle)) $;

--| 'Less than or equal' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 10-Mar-2006.)
theorem lemuldiv2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co C A2 cmul) B2 cle) (wbr A2 (co B2 C cdiv) cle)) $;

--| The reciprocal of both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 26-Sep-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem ltrec (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co c1 B2 cdiv) (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt)) $;

--| The reciprocal of both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 3-Oct-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lerec (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co c1 B2 cdiv) (co c1 A2 cdiv) cle)) $;

--| Lemma for ~ lt2msq . (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lt2msq1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wcel B2 cr) (wbr A2 B2 clt)) (wbr (co A2 A2 cmul) (co B2 B2 cmul) clt) $;

--| Two nonnegative numbers compare the same as their squares. (Contributed by Roy F. Longton, 8-Aug-2005.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem lt2msq (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 cle))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 A2 cmul) (co B2 B2 cmul) clt)) $;

--| Division of a positive number by both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 27-Apr-2005.)
theorem ltdiv2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co C B2 cdiv) (co C A2 cdiv) clt)) $;

--| Reciprocal swap in a 'less than' relation. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem ltrec1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wb (wbr (co c1 A2 cdiv) B2 clt) (wbr (co c1 B2 cdiv) A2 clt)) $;

--| Reciprocal swap in a 'less than or equal to' relation. (Contributed by NM, 24-Feb-2005.)
theorem lerec2 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wb (wbr A2 (co c1 B2 cdiv) cle) (wbr B2 (co c1 A2 cdiv) cle)) $;

--| Invert ratios of positive numbers and swap their ordering. (Contributed by NM, 9-Jan-2006.)
theorem ledivdiv (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt))) (wa (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt)) (wa (wcel D cr) (wbr cc0 D clt)))) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) (co C D cdiv) cle) (wbr (co D C cdiv) (co B2 A2 cdiv) cle)) $;

--| Division of a positive number by both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 10-Jan-2006.)
theorem lediv2 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co C B2 cdiv) (co C A2 cdiv) cle)) $;

--| Swap denominator with other side of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 3-Oct-1999.)
theorem ltdiv23 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) C clt) (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) B2 clt)) $;

--| Swap denominator with other side of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 30-May-2005.)
theorem lediv23 (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C clt))) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) C cle) (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) B2 cle)) $;

--| Comparison of ratio of two nonnegative numbers. (Contributed by NM, 31-Dec-2005.)
theorem lediv12a (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr A2 B2 cle))) (wa (wa (wcel C cr) (wcel D cr)) (wa (wbr cc0 C clt) (wbr C D cle)))) (wbr (co A2 D cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) cle) $;

--| Division of both sides of 'less than or equal to' into a nonnegative number. (Contributed by Paul Chapman, 7-Sep-2007.)
theorem lediv2a (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wa (wcel C cr) (wbr cc0 C cle))) (wbr A2 B2 cle)) (wbr (co C B2 cdiv) (co C A2 cdiv) cle) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive number less than 1 is greater than 1. (Contributed by NM, 23-Feb-2005.)
theorem reclt1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wb (wbr A2 c1 clt) (wbr c1 (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt)) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive number greater than 1 is less than 1. (Contributed by NM, 28-Dec-2005.)
theorem recgt1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wb (wbr c1 A2 clt) (wbr (co c1 A2 cdiv) c1 clt)) $;

--| The reciprocal of a number greater than 1 is positive and less than 1. (Contributed by NM, 23-Feb-2005.)
theorem recgt1i (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr c1 A2 clt)) (wa (wbr cc0 (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt) (wbr (co c1 A2 cdiv) c1 clt)) $;

--| Construct a number less than 1 from any nonnegative number. (Contributed by NM, 30-Dec-2005.)
theorem recp1lt1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wbr (co A2 (co c1 A2 caddc) cdiv) c1 clt) $;

--| Given a positive number ` A ` , construct a new positive number less than both ` A ` and 1. (Contributed by NM, 28-Dec-2005.)
theorem recreclt (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 clt)) (wa (wbr (co c1 (co c1 (co c1 A2 cdiv) caddc) cdiv) c1 clt) (wbr (co c1 (co c1 (co c1 A2 cdiv) caddc) cdiv) A2 clt)) $;

--| The square function on nonnegative reals is monotonic. (Contributed by NM, 3-Aug-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem le2msq (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 cle))) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 A2 cmul) (co B2 B2 cmul) cle)) $;

--| The square of a nonnegative number is a one-to-one function. (Contributed by NM, 29-Jul-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem msq11 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 cle))) (wb (wceq (co A2 A2 cmul) (co B2 B2 cmul)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| Less-than-or-equal-to and division relation. (Lemma for computing upper bounds of products. The "+ 1" prevents division by zero.) (Contributed by NM, 28-Sep-2005.)
theorem ledivp1 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle)) (wa (wcel B2 cr) (wbr cc0 B2 cle))) (wbr (co (co A2 (co B2 c1 caddc) cdiv) B2 cmul) A2 cle) $;

--| If a nonnegative number is less than any positive number, it is zero. (Contributed by NM, 11-Feb-2006.)
theorem squeeze0 {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (w3a (wcel A2 cr) (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wral x3 (wi (wbr cc0 (cv x3) clt) (wbr A2 (cv x3) clt)) cr)) (wceq A2 cc0) $;

--| A number is less than itself plus 1. (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-2001.)
theorem ltp1i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wbr A2 (co A2 c1 caddc) clt $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive number is positive. Exercise 4 of [Apostol] p. 21. (Contributed by NM, 15-May-1999.)
theorem recgt0i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive number is positive. Exercise 4 of [Apostol] p. 21. (Contributed by NM, 15-May-1999.)
theorem recgt0ii (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 A2 clt $ >
  $ wbr cc0 (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt $;

--| Infer that a multiplicand is positive from a nonnegative multiplier and positive product. (Contributed by NM, 15-May-1999.)
theorem prodgt0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) clt)) (wbr cc0 B2 clt) $;

--| Infer that a multiplicand is nonnegative from a positive multiplier and nonnegative product. (Contributed by NM, 2-Jul-2005.)
theorem prodge0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cmul) cle)) (wbr cc0 B2 cle) $;

--| The ratio of two positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 16-May-1999.)
theorem divgt0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cdiv) clt) $;

--| The ratio of nonnegative and positive numbers is nonnegative. (Contributed by NM, 12-Aug-1999.)
theorem divge0i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cdiv) cle) $;

--| The reciprocal of both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 15-Sep-1999.)
theorem ltreci (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co c1 B2 cdiv) (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt)) $;

--| The reciprocal of both sides of 'less than or equal to'. (Contributed by NM, 16-Sep-1999.)
theorem lereci (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 B2 clt)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co c1 B2 cdiv) (co c1 A2 cdiv) cle)) $;

--| The square function on nonnegative reals is strictly monotonic. (Contributed by NM, 3-Aug-1999.)
theorem lt2msqi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 cle)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 A2 cmul) (co B2 B2 cmul) clt)) $;

--| The square function on nonnegative reals is monotonic. (Contributed by NM, 2-Aug-1999.)
theorem le2msqi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 cle)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 A2 cmul) (co B2 B2 cmul) cle)) $;

--| The square of a nonnegative number is a one-to-one function. (Contributed by NM, 29-Jul-1999.)
theorem msq11i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 A2 cle) (wbr cc0 B2 cle)) (wb (wceq (co A2 A2 cmul) (co B2 B2 cmul)) (wceq A2 B2)) $;

--| The ratio of two positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 16-May-1999.)
theorem divgt0i2i (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 B2 clt $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 A2 clt) (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cdiv) clt) $;

--| The reciprocal of both sides of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 15-Sep-1999.)
theorem ltrecii (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 A2 clt $ >
  $ wbr cc0 B2 clt $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co c1 B2 cdiv) (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt) $;

--| The ratio of two positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by NM, 18-May-1999.)
theorem divgt0ii (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 A2 clt $ >
  $ wbr cc0 B2 clt $ >
  $ wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cdiv) clt $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than' by a positive number. Theorem I.19 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 16-May-1999.)
theorem ltmul1i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 C clt) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) clt)) $;

--| Division of both sides of 'less than' by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 16-May-1999.)
theorem ltdiv1i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 C clt) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) clt)) $;

--| 'Less than' relationship between division and multiplication. (Contributed by NM, 12-Oct-1999.)
theorem ltmuldivi (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 C clt) (wb (wbr (co A2 C cmul) B2 clt) (wbr A2 (co B2 C cdiv) clt)) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than' by a positive number. Theorem I.19 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 16-May-1999.)
theorem ltmul2i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 C clt) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul) clt)) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than or equal to' by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 2-Aug-1999.)
theorem lemul1i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 C clt) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cle)) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than or equal to' by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1999.)
theorem lemul2i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wi (wbr cc0 C clt) (wb (wbr A2 B2 cle) (wbr (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul) cle)) $;

--| Swap denominator with other side of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 26-Sep-1999.)
theorem ltdiv23i (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wi (wa (wbr cc0 B2 clt) (wbr cc0 C clt)) (wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) C clt) (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) B2 clt)) $;

--| Swap denominator with other side of 'less than'. (Contributed by NM, 26-Sep-1999.)
theorem ltdiv23ii (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 B2 clt $ >
  $ wbr cc0 C clt $ >
  $ wb (wbr (co A2 B2 cdiv) C clt) (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) B2 clt) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than' by a positive number. Theorem I.19 of [Apostol] p. 20. (Contributed by NM, 16-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Paul Chapman, 25-Jan-2008.)
theorem ltmul1ii (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 C clt $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) clt) $;

--| Division of both sides of 'less than' by a positive number. (Contributed by NM, 16-May-1999.)
theorem ltdiv1ii (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wcel A2 cr $ >
  $ wcel B2 cr $ >
  $ wcel C cr $ >
  $ wbr cc0 C clt $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wbr (co A2 C cdiv) (co B2 C cdiv) clt) $;

--| A number is less than itself plus 1. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem ltp1d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 (co A2 c1 caddc) clt) $;

--| A number is less than or equal to itself plus 1. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem lep1d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 (co A2 c1 caddc) cle) $;

--| A number minus 1 is less than itself. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem ltm1d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 c1 cmin) A2 clt) $;

--| A number minus 1 is less than or equal to itself. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem lem1d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 c1 cmin) A2 cle) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive number is positive. Exercise 4 of [Apostol] p. 21. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem recgt0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt) $;

--| The ratio of two positive numbers is positive. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem divgt0d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 (co A2 B2 cdiv) clt) $;

--| The product of two numbers greater than 1 is greater than 1. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem mulgt1d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 A2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 (co A2 B2 cmul) clt) $;

--| Multiplication by a number greater than or equal to 1. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem lemulge11d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 (co A2 B2 cmul) cle) $;

--| Multiplication by a number greater than or equal to 1. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem lemulge12d (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 (co B2 A2 cmul) cle) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than or equal to' by a nonnegative number. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem lemul1ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 C cmul) cle) $;

--| Multiplication of both sides of 'less than or equal to' by a nonnegative number. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem lemul2ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co C A2 cmul) (co C B2 cmul) cle) $;

--| Comparison of product of two positive numbers. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem ltmul12ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C D clt) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 D cmul) clt) $;

--| Comparison of product of two nonnegative numbers. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem lemul12ad (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 C cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C D cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 D cmul) cle) $;

--| Comparison of product of two nonnegative numbers. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 28-May-2016.)
theorem lemul12bd (ph: wff) (A2 B2 C D: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel C cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel D cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 D cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 B2 cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr C D cle) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr (co A2 C cmul) (co B2 D cmul) cle) $;

--| The real representation of complex numbers is apart from zero iff one of its terms is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 5-Mar-2020.)
theorem crap0 (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel B2 cr)) (wb (wo (wbr A2 cc0 cap) (wbr B2 cc0 cap)) (wbr (co A2 (co ci B2 cmul) caddc) cc0 cap)) $;

--| The real part of a complex number is unique. Proposition 10-1.3 of [Gleason] p. 130. (Contributed by NM, 9-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem creur {x3 y1: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wreu x3 (wrex y1 (wceq A2 (co (cv x3) (co ci (cv y1) cmul) caddc)) cr) cr) $;

--| The imaginary part of a complex number is unique. Proposition 10-1.3 of [Gleason] p. 130. (Contributed by NM, 9-May-1999.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem creui {x3 y1: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wreu y1 (wrex x3 (wceq A2 (co (cv x3) (co ci (cv y1) cmul) caddc)) cr) cr) $;

--| The complex conjugate of a complex number is unique. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 6-Nov-2013.)
theorem cju {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wreu x3 (wa (wcel (co A2 (cv x3) caddc) cr) (wcel (co ci (co A2 (cv x3) cmin) cmul) cr)) cc) $;

--| Extend class notation to include the class of positive integers.
term cn: class;

--| Definition of the set of positive integers. For naming consistency with the Metamath Proof Explorer usages should refer to ~ dfnn2 instead. (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 12-Sep-2013.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 3-May-2014.) (New usage is discouraged.)
axiom df_inn {x3 y1: setvar}:
  $ wceq cn (cint (cab x3 (wa (wcel c1 (cv x3)) (wral y1 (wcel (co (cv y1) c1 caddc) (cv x3)) (cv x3))))) $;

--| Definition of the set of positive integers. Another name for ~ df-inn . (Contributed by Jeff Hankins, 12-Sep-2013.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 3-May-2014.)
theorem dfnn2 {x3 y1: setvar}:
  $ wceq cn (cint (cab x3 (wa (wcel c1 (cv x3)) (wral y1 (wcel (co (cv y1) c1 caddc) (cv x3)) (cv x3))))) $;

--| Peano's inductive postulate. Theorem I.36 (principle of mathematical induction) of [Apostol] p. 34. (Contributed by NM, 10-Jan-1997.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 17-Nov-2014.)
theorem peano5nni {x3: setvar} (A2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel c1 A2) (wral x3 (wcel (co (cv x3) c1 caddc) A2) A2)) (wss cn A2) $;

--| The positive integers are a subset of the reals. (Contributed by NM, 10-Jan-1997.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 16-Jun-2013.)
theorem nnssre:
  $ wss cn cr $;

--| The positive integers are a subset of the complex numbers. (Contributed by NM, 2-Aug-2004.)
theorem nnsscn:
  $ wss cn cc $;

--| The set of positive integers exists. (Contributed by NM, 3-Oct-1999.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 17-Nov-2014.)
theorem nnex:
  $ wcel cn cvv $;

--| A positive integer is a real number. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1999.)
theorem nnre (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wcel A2 cr) $;

--| A positive integer is a complex number. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1999.)
theorem nncn (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wcel A2 cc) $;

--| A positive integer is a real number. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1999.)
theorem nnrei (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cn $ >
  $ wcel A2 cr $;

--| A positive integer is a complex number. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1999.)
theorem nncni (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cn $ >
  $ wcel A2 cc $;

--| Peano postulate: 1 is a positive integer. (Contributed by NM, 11-Jan-1997.)
theorem _1nn:
  $ wcel c1 cn $;

--| Peano postulate: a successor of a positive integer is a positive integer. (Contributed by NM, 11-Jan-1997.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 17-Nov-2014.)
theorem peano2nn (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wcel (co A2 c1 caddc) cn) $;

--| A positive integer is a real number. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnred (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $;

--| A positive integer is a complex number. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nncnd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cc) $;

--| Peano postulate: a successor of a positive integer is a positive integer. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem peano2nnd (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 c1 caddc) cn) $;

--| Principle of Mathematical Induction (inference schema). The first four hypotheses give us the substitution instances we need; the last two are the basis and the induction step. See ~ nnaddcl for an example of its use. This is an alternative for Metamath 100 proof #74. (Contributed by NM, 10-Jan-1997.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 16-Jun-2013.)
theorem nnind {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff x3) (ps ch th ta: wff y1) (A2: class y1):
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) c1) (wb ph ps) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) (cv y1)) (wb ph ch) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) (co (cv y1) c1 caddc)) (wb ph th) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) A2) (wb ph ta) $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wcel (cv y1) cn) (wi ch th) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) ta $;

--| Principle of Mathematical Induction (inference schema). The last four hypotheses give us the substitution instances we need; the first two are the induction step and the basis. This ALT version of ~ nnind has a different hypothesis order. It may be easier to use with the metamath program's Proof Assistant, because "MM-PA> assign last" will be applied to the substitution instances first. We may eventually use this one as the official version. You may use either version. After the proof is complete, the ALT version can be changed to the non-ALT version with "MM-PA> minimize nnind /allow". (Contributed by NM, 7-Dec-2005.) (New usage is discouraged.) (Proof modification is discouraged.)
theorem nnindALT {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff x3) (ps ch th ta: wff y1) (A2: class y1):
  $ wi (wcel (cv y1) cn) (wi ch th) $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) c1) (wb ph ps) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) (cv y1)) (wb ph ch) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) (co (cv y1) c1 caddc)) (wb ph th) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) A2) (wb ph ta) $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) ta $;

--| Every positive integer is one or a successor. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 16-May-2014.)
theorem nn1m1nn (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wo (wceq A2 c1) (wcel (co A2 c1 cmin) cn)) $;

--| If a statement holds for 1 and also holds for a successor, it holds for all positive integers. The first three hypotheses give us the substitution instances we need; the last two show that it holds for 1 and for a successor. (Contributed by NM, 11-Oct-2004.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 16-May-2014.)
theorem nn1suc {x3 y1: setvar} (ph: wff x3) (ps ch th: wff y1) (A2: class):
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) c1) (wb ph ps) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) (co (cv y1) c1 caddc)) (wb ph ch) $ >
  $ wi (wceq (cv x3) A2) (wb ph th) $ >
  $ ps $ >
  $ wi (wcel (cv y1) cn) ch $ >
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) th $;

--| Closure of addition of positive integers, proved by induction on the second addend. (Contributed by NM, 12-Jan-1997.)
theorem nnaddcl (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cn) (wcel B2 cn)) (wcel (co A2 B2 caddc) cn) $;

--| Closure of multiplication of positive integers. (Contributed by NM, 12-Jan-1997.)
theorem nnmulcl (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cn) (wcel B2 cn)) (wcel (co A2 B2 cmul) cn) $;

--| Closure of multiplication of positive integers. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 18-Feb-2014.)
theorem nnmulcli (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cn $ >
  $ wcel B2 cn $ >
  $ wcel (co A2 B2 cmul) cn $;

--| A positive integer is one or greater. (Contributed by NM, 25-Aug-1999.)
theorem nnge1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wbr c1 A2 cle) $;

--| A positive integer is less than or equal to one iff it is equal to one. (Contributed by NM, 3-Apr-2005.)
theorem nnle1eq1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wb (wbr A2 c1 cle) (wceq A2 c1)) $;

--| A positive integer is positive. (Contributed by NM, 26-Sep-1999.)
theorem nngt0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wbr cc0 A2 clt) $;

--| A positive integer is not less than one. (Contributed by NM, 18-Jan-2004.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnnlt1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wn (wbr A2 c1 clt)) $;

--| Zero is not a positive integer. (Contributed by NM, 25-Aug-1999.)
theorem _0nnn:
  $ wn (wcel cc0 cn) $;

--| A positive integer is nonzero. (Contributed by NM, 27-Sep-1999.)
theorem nnne0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wne A2 cc0) $;

--| A positive integer is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 8-Mar-2020.)
theorem nnap0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $;

--| A positive integer is positive (inference version). (Contributed by NM, 17-Sep-1999.)
theorem nngt0i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cn $ >
  $ wbr cc0 A2 clt $;

--| A positive integer is nonzero (inference version). (Contributed by NM, 25-Aug-1999.)
theorem nnne0i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cn $ >
  $ wne A2 cc0 $;

--| There exists a positive integer greater than or equal to any two others. (Contributed by NM, 18-Aug-1999.)
theorem nn2ge {x3: setvar} (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cn) (wcel B2 cn)) (wrex x3 (wa (wbr A2 (cv x3) cle) (wbr B2 (cv x3) cle)) cn) $;

--| A positive integer is either one or greater than one. This is for ` NN ` ; ~ 0elnn is a similar theorem for ` _om ` (the natural numbers as ordinals). (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 7-Mar-2020.)
theorem nn1gt1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wo (wceq A2 c1) (wbr c1 A2 clt)) $;

--| A positive integer is greater than one iff it is not equal to one. (Contributed by NM, 7-Oct-2004.)
theorem nngt1ne1 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wb (wbr c1 A2 clt) (wne A2 c1)) $;

--| The quotient of a real and a positive integer is real. (Contributed by NM, 28-Nov-2008.)
theorem nndivre (A2 N: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cr) (wcel N cn)) (wcel (co A2 N cdiv) cr) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive integer is real. (Contributed by NM, 8-Feb-2008.)
theorem nnrecre (N: class):
  $ wi (wcel N cn) (wcel (co c1 N cdiv) cr) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive integer is positive. (Contributed by NM, 25-Aug-1999.)
theorem nnrecgt0 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cn) (wbr cc0 (co c1 A2 cdiv) clt) $;

--| Subtraction of positive integers. (Contributed by NM, 20-Aug-2001.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 16-May-2014.)
theorem nnsub (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cn) (wcel B2 cn)) (wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wcel (co B2 A2 cmin) cn)) $;

--| Subtraction of positive integers. (Contributed by NM, 19-Aug-2001.)
theorem nnsubi (A2 B2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cn $ >
  $ wcel B2 cn $ >
  $ wb (wbr A2 B2 clt) (wcel (co B2 A2 cmin) cn) $;

--| Two ways to express " ` A ` divides ` B ` " for positive integers. (Contributed by NM, 3-Feb-2004.) (Proof shortened by Mario Carneiro, 16-May-2014.)
theorem nndiv {x3: setvar} (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi (wa (wcel A2 cn) (wcel B2 cn)) (wb (wrex x3 (wceq (co A2 (cv x3) cmul) B2) cn) (wcel (co B2 A2 cdiv) cn)) $;

--| Transitive property of divisibility: if ` A ` divides ` B ` and ` B ` divides ` C ` , then ` A ` divides ` C ` . Typically, ` C ` would be an integer, although the theorem holds for complex ` C ` . (Contributed by NM, 3-May-2005.)
theorem nndivtr (A2 B2 C: class):
  $ wi (wa (w3a (wcel A2 cn) (wcel B2 cn) (wcel C cc)) (wa (wcel (co B2 A2 cdiv) cn) (wcel (co C B2 cdiv) cn))) (wcel (co C A2 cdiv) cn) $;

--| A positive integer is one or greater. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnge1d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr c1 A2 cle) $;

--| A positive integer is positive. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nngt0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr cc0 A2 clt) $;

--| A positive integer is nonzero. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnne0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wne A2 cc0) $;

--| A positive integer is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 25-Aug-2021.)
theorem nnap0d (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wbr A2 cc0 cap) $;

--| The reciprocal of a positive integer is real. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnrecred (ph: wff) (A2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co c1 A2 cdiv) cr) $;

--| Closure of addition of positive integers. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnaddcld (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 B2 caddc) cn) $;

--| Closure of multiplication of positive integers. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nnmulcld (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 B2 cmul) cn) $;

--| A positive integer is one or greater. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.)
theorem nndivred (ph: wff) (A2 B2: class):
  $ wi ph (wcel A2 cr) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel B2 cn) $ >
  $ wi ph (wcel (co A2 B2 cdiv) cr) $;

--| Extend class notation to include the number 2.
term c2: class;

--| Extend class notation to include the number 3.
term c3: class;

--| Extend class notation to include the number 4.
term c4: class;

--| Extend class notation to include the number 5.
term c5: class;

--| Extend class notation to include the number 6.
term c6: class;

--| Extend class notation to include the number 7.
term c7: class;

--| Extend class notation to include the number 8.
term c8: class;

--| Extend class notation to include the number 9.
term c9: class;

--| Extend class notation to include the number 10.
term c10: class;

--| Define the number 2. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
axiom df_2:
  $ wceq c2 (co c1 c1 caddc) $;

--| Define the number 3. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
axiom df_3:
  $ wceq c3 (co c2 c1 caddc) $;

--| Define the number 4. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
axiom df_4:
  $ wceq c4 (co c3 c1 caddc) $;

--| Define the number 5. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
axiom df_5:
  $ wceq c5 (co c4 c1 caddc) $;

--| Define the number 6. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
axiom df_6:
  $ wceq c6 (co c5 c1 caddc) $;

--| Define the number 7. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
axiom df_7:
  $ wceq c7 (co c6 c1 caddc) $;

--| Define the number 8. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
axiom df_8:
  $ wceq c8 (co c7 c1 caddc) $;

--| Define the number 9. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
axiom df_9:
  $ wceq c9 (co c8 c1 caddc) $;

--| Define the number 10. See remarks under ~ df-2 . (Contributed by NM, 5-Feb-2007.)
axiom df_10:
  $ wceq c10 (co c9 c1 caddc) $;

--| ` 0 =/= 1 ` (common case). See aso ~ 1ap0 . (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _0ne1:
  $ wne cc0 c1 $;

--| ` 1 =/= 0 ` . See aso ~ 1ap0 . (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem _1ne0:
  $ wne c1 cc0 $;

--| ` ( 1 - 1 ) = 0 ` (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 7-Jul-2016.)
theorem _1m1e0:
  $ wceq (co c1 c1 cmin) cc0 $;

--| The number 2 is real. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _2re:
  $ wcel c2 cr $;

--| The number 2 is a complex number. (Contributed by NM, 30-Jul-2004.)
theorem _2cn:
  $ wcel c2 cc $;

--| 2 is a set (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _2ex:
  $ wcel c2 cvv $;

--| 2 is a complex number, deductive form (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _2cnd (ph: wff):
  $ wi ph (wcel c2 cc) $;

--| The number 3 is real. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _3re:
  $ wcel c3 cr $;

--| The number 3 is a complex number. (Contributed by FL, 17-Oct-2010.)
theorem _3cn:
  $ wcel c3 cc $;

--| 3 is a set (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _3ex:
  $ wcel c3 cvv $;

--| The number 4 is real. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _4re:
  $ wcel c4 cr $;

--| The number 4 is a complex number. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 7-Jul-2016.)
theorem _4cn:
  $ wcel c4 cc $;

--| The number 5 is real. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _5re:
  $ wcel c5 cr $;

--| The number 5 is complex. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _5cn:
  $ wcel c5 cc $;

--| The number 6 is real. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _6re:
  $ wcel c6 cr $;

--| The number 6 is complex. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _6cn:
  $ wcel c6 cc $;

--| The number 7 is real. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _7re:
  $ wcel c7 cr $;

--| The number 7 is complex. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _7cn:
  $ wcel c7 cc $;

--| The number 8 is real. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _8re:
  $ wcel c8 cr $;

--| The number 8 is complex. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _8cn:
  $ wcel c8 cc $;

--| The number 9 is real. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _9re:
  $ wcel c9 cr $;

--| The number 9 is complex. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _9cn:
  $ wcel c9 cc $;

--| The number 10 is real. (Contributed by NM, 5-Feb-2007.)
theorem _10re:
  $ wcel c10 cr $;

--| Zero is nonnegative. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 7-Jul-2016.)
theorem _0le0:
  $ wbr cc0 cc0 cle $;

--| 0 is less than or equal to 2. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 7-Dec-2018.)
theorem _0le2:
  $ wbr cc0 c2 cle $;

--| The number 2 is positive. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _2pos:
  $ wbr cc0 c2 clt $;

--| The number 2 is nonzero. (Contributed by NM, 9-Nov-2007.)
theorem _2ne0:
  $ wne c2 cc0 $;

--| The number 2 is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Mar-2020.)
theorem _2ap0:
  $ wbr c2 cc0 cap $;

--| The number 3 is positive. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _3pos:
  $ wbr cc0 c3 clt $;

--| The number 3 is nonzero. (Contributed by FL, 17-Oct-2010.) (Proof shortened by Andrew Salmon, 7-May-2011.)
theorem _3ne0:
  $ wne c3 cc0 $;

--| The number 3 is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 10-Oct-2021.)
theorem _3ap0:
  $ wbr c3 cc0 cap $;

--| The number 4 is positive. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _4pos:
  $ wbr cc0 c4 clt $;

--| The number 4 is nonzero. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 5-Dec-2018.)
theorem _4ne0:
  $ wne c4 cc0 $;

--| The number 4 is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 10-Oct-2021.)
theorem _4ap0:
  $ wbr c4 cc0 cap $;

--| The number 5 is positive. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _5pos:
  $ wbr cc0 c5 clt $;

--| The number 6 is positive. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _6pos:
  $ wbr cc0 c6 clt $;

--| The number 7 is positive. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _7pos:
  $ wbr cc0 c7 clt $;

--| The number 8 is positive. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _8pos:
  $ wbr cc0 c8 clt $;

--| The number 9 is positive. (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _9pos:
  $ wbr cc0 c9 clt $;

--| The number 10 is positive. (Contributed by NM, 5-Feb-2007.)
theorem _10pos:
  $ wbr cc0 c10 clt $;

--| -1 is a complex number (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 7-Jul-2016.)
theorem neg1cn:
  $ wcel (cneg c1) cc $;

--| -1 is a real number (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 5-Dec-2018.)
theorem neg1rr:
  $ wcel (cneg c1) cr $;

--| -1 is nonzero (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem neg1ne0:
  $ wne (cneg c1) cc0 $;

--| -1 is less than 0 (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem neg1lt0:
  $ wbr (cneg c1) cc0 clt $;

--| -1 is apart from zero. (Contributed by Jim Kingdon, 9-Jun-2020.)
theorem neg1ap0:
  $ wbr (cneg c1) cc0 cap $;

--| ` -u -u 1 ` is 1 (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem negneg1e1:
  $ wceq (cneg (cneg c1)) c1 $;

--| ` 1 + -u 1 ` is 0 (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _1pneg1e0:
  $ wceq (co c1 (cneg c1) caddc) cc0 $;

--| 0 minus 0 equals 0 (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _0m0e0:
  $ wceq (co cc0 cc0 cmin) cc0 $;

--| 1 - 0 = 1 (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _1m0e1:
  $ wceq (co c1 cc0 cmin) c1 $;

--| 0 + 1 = 1. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 7-Jul-2016.)
theorem _0p1e1:
  $ wceq (co cc0 c1 caddc) c1 $;

--| 1 + 0 = 1. (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _1p0e1:
  $ wceq (co c1 cc0 caddc) c1 $;

--| 1 + 1 = 2. (Contributed by NM, 1-Apr-2008.)
theorem _1p1e2:
  $ wceq (co c1 c1 caddc) c2 $;

--| 2 - 1 = 1. The result is on the right-hand-side to be consistent with similar proofs like ~ 4p4e8 . (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 4-Jan-2017.)
theorem _2m1e1:
  $ wceq (co c2 c1 cmin) c1 $;

--| 1 = 2 - 1 (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _1e2m1:
  $ wceq c1 (co c2 c1 cmin) $;

--| 3 - 1 = 2. (Contributed by FL, 17-Oct-2010.) (Revised by NM, 10-Dec-2017.)
theorem _3m1e2:
  $ wceq (co c3 c1 cmin) c2 $;

--| Two plus two equals four. For more information, see "2+2=4 Trivia" on the Metamath Proof Explorer Home Page: ~ http://us.metamath.org/mpeuni/mmset.html#trivia . (Contributed by NM, 27-May-1999.)
theorem _2p2e4:
  $ wceq (co c2 c2 caddc) c4 $;

--| Two times a number. (Contributed by NM, 10-Oct-2004.) (Revised by Mario Carneiro, 27-May-2016.) (Proof shortened by AV, 26-Feb-2020.)
theorem _2times (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wceq (co c2 A2 cmul) (co A2 A2 caddc)) $;

--| A number times 2. (Contributed by NM, 16-Oct-2007.)
theorem times2 (A2: class):
  $ wi (wcel A2 cc) (wceq (co A2 c2 cmul) (co A2 A2 caddc)) $;

--| Two times a number. (Contributed by NM, 1-Aug-1999.)
theorem _2timesi (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wceq (co c2 A2 cmul) (co A2 A2 caddc) $;

--| A number times 2. (Contributed by NM, 11-May-2004.)
theorem times2i (A2: class):
  $ wcel A2 cc $ >
  $ wceq (co A2 c2 cmul) (co A2 A2 caddc) $;

--| 2 divided by 2 is 1 (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _2div2e1:
  $ wceq (co c2 c2 cdiv) c1 $;

--| 2 + 1 = 3. (Contributed by Mario Carneiro, 18-Apr-2015.)
theorem _2p1e3:
  $ wceq (co c2 c1 caddc) c3 $;

--| 1 + 2 = 3 (common case). (Contributed by David A. Wheeler, 8-Dec-2018.)
theorem _1p2e3:
  $ wceq (co c1 c2 caddc) c3 $;

